    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE. `GameRenderCommand.h/.cpp` introduces `IBackend` plus explicit entity/object/immediate-3D/immediate-2D roles such as `OBJECT_DRAW_VR_WEAPON`, `IMMEDIATE3D_DRAW_VR_HAND`, `IMMEDIATE3D_DRAW_VR_LASER`, `IMMEDIATE3D_DRAW_WATER`, `IMMEDIATE2D_DRAW_RADAR` and `IMMEDIATE2D_DRAW_POST_FX`. The compatibility backend still executes the original RenderWare calls immediately, preserving order/state, while the Vulkan path can consume role metadata for water/depth/UI policy. This is a strong migration strategy when a flat engine is too large to rewrite at once: first make draw intent explicit, then change the backend behind that seam.",
