    "summary": "Rather than a single instant switch from \"runtime-hooked binary\" to \"full source,\" this project shows decompilation as a gradual spectrum: only a documented percentage of the game's functions have been re-implemented and verified so far, and each one can be toggled on or off individually while debugging.",
    "details": "The base project explicitly is not attempting full matching decompilation — it re-implements individual functions well enough to replace them, verified with Ghidra and an assembly-level debugger, and tracks percentage-complete over time (documented at roughly 30% in late 2023 growing past 70% by mid-2026). A `// 0xADDRESS HOOK` comment convention lets a developer mark exactly which reimplemented functions are actually swapped in versus kept as reference-only, which is a useful methodology in itself for any incremental decompilation-based mod: partial source access can still enable targeted VR-relevant changes (like the rendering functions) years before the whole engine is understood. The PCVR fork layers OpenXR stereo rendering, head tracking, and Quest controller support on top of this partially-decompiled base once enough of the rendering path was understood to modify safely.",
