    "details": "Emulator-level VR is a genuinely different category from the runtime-injection and source-decompilation patterns documented elsewhere in this registry: the leverage point is the emulator's own rendering/input pipeline rather than any single game's compiled code, which in principle could let VR plumbing carry over to other titles under the same emulator core — though the arm-cannon tracking, targeting integration, and texture-swap tooling here are game-aware features layered on top, not a generic 'every GameCube game gets VR for free' claim. The easy cannon-texture-swapping tool and one-click height calibration are both simple, reusable quality-of-life patterns worth borrowing for any VR mod's onboarding flow, regardless of technique. Built on iChris4's Dolphin ReduX development branch, with the Metroid Prime modding community credited for prior research this project built on.",
