    "details": "For a Unity project a modder can actually rebuild or patch (source access, or a BepInEx-style plugin hook into a shipped game), enabling this plugin through Project Settings -> XR Plugin Management makes head and controller tracking close to 'free' the same way UEVR makes it free for Unreal titles: a TrackedPoseDriver component gives tracked camera pose immediately, and a separate SteamVR Input System package (steamvr_unity_plugin) adds real controller button/pose input plus a working example interaction scene to build from. The critical practical split this clarifies for anyone modding an already-compiled Unity game (not a source project): this plugin only helps when the target's Unity project itself can be modified to register it — for a shipped, closed Unity binary, a modder is normally forced into exactly the kind of virtual-gamepad-emulation workaround documented elsewhere in this registry (PEAK's ViGEmBus approach) precisely because the XR Plugin Management UI isn't reachable at all. As of this writing Valve states it is moving toward OpenXR support directly in future versions of this plugin rather than remaining OpenVR-only.",
