    "summary": "Instead of rotating the camera to make gunfire follow the controller, the profile changes Dead Island 2 projectile-spawner policy to raycast from the weapon muzzle and disables camera/auto-aim corrections that would bend the shot back toward the flatscreen aim model.",
    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE (`scripts/helpers/ranged.lua`). `applyRangedWeaponMuzzleAim()` walks the local pawn → `BPC_Player_PaperDoll` → weapon slot → `RangedWeaponModulesComponent`, then patches the selected projectile spawner/fire mode. `RaycastType` is set to `ETargetPointRaycastType_RaycastFromMuzzle`; `LocalUserMuzzleAlignmentToleranceDegrees` is widened to 180° and the local muzzle-alignment push remains enabled. `LaunchAdjustmentHandler.MaxAdjustScreenSpacePercentage` is set to 0 and `bUseCachedPlayerAutoAimResults` is disabled. Reusable rule: if native firing is already correct except for a camera-owned origin/direction, retarget the native ray source rather than replacing fire/damage/ammo logic.",
