    "summary": "A UEVR profile plus native C++ plugin that uses engine-level callbacks for render, camera, interaction and scripted-sequence fixes that are awkward or impossible to express as a simple Lua profile.",
    "details": "The public source documents a clear division of labor: the UEVR profile supplies the general injection/configuration layer, while the compiled C++ plugin handles game-specific behavior such as 6DOF weapon alignment, interaction mode, physical crouching, melee gesture thresholds, culling-FOV correction, per-eye transparency fixes, first-person scripted-sequence repairs and UI/cutscene state. The important architecture lesson is selective escalation: keep ordinary VR configuration in the profile, but move features that require deeper engine access into a native plugin. Cyberspace is deliberately given a different control scheme rather than forced into free 6DOF, showing that sub-modes with incompatible camera/physics assumptions may need their own VR interaction model. The plugin also treats culling and first-person animation as independent compatibility surfaces: fixing the headset camera alone does not guarantee correct visibility or scripted animation. A maintained successor, SystemReShock-UEVR-Plugin, demonstrates the same profile-plus-native-plugin pattern while moving additional configuration into a persistent INI file and keeping optional physical-melee/player-arm changes as separate scripts/PAK content.",
    "blockers": "Requires a compatible UEVR nightly and careful profile replacement. Native-plugin changes require a C++ build/UEVR plugin toolchain, while optional PAK/Lua augmentations remain separate from the core plugin. The public source does not establish a complete low-level renderer/frame-timing sequence.",
    "sourceLinks": "https://github.com/Ashok0/SystemShock-UEVR, https://github.com/gwizdek/SystemReShock-UEVR-Plugin",
    "submittedBy": "seed",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-05"
