    "details": "Scrap Mechanic Native VR focuses on translating the game's sandbox interaction vocabulary rather than only attaching a VR camera. The current release is guarded to a specific Steam build and refuses unknown versions rather than applying unsafe renderer hooks. It provides native stereo OpenXR rendering, HMD tracking and a desktop eye mirror. Quest Touch controllers and Meta optical hand tracking are both supported. Locomotion is HMD-relative with horizontal snap/smooth turning and a seated mode using the game's Strict Follow Camera. Recenter can realign yaw, pitch, roll and floor height. The tracked mechanic hands remain visible and tools/held objects follow the hands. The interaction layer covers lift placement, block placement/removal, painting, welding, connection dragging, switches, buttons, guns and elevators. Existing game menus are surfaced as floating VR panels with pointer/click/hold/drag interaction. Hammer swings are motion-driven and gun barrel targeting is hand-driven; tool laser pointers are likewise attached to the tracked interaction hand. The installer is deliberately conservative: it verifies the supported game build, preserves backups/conflicts, can repair and fully restore the installation. For an LLM, the important pattern is not only 'find a render hook' but 'make the installer and runtime version gate fail closed' because native hooks into a fast-moving game are otherwise likely to corrupt or crash newer builds.",
