    "details": "SoDVR is a useful Unity IL2CPP pattern because it shows the packaging boundary required when the game did not ship with the exact XR runtime stack the mod needs. The release installs a BepInEx plugin plus a preloader component and a native openxr_loader.dll under RuntimeDeps/Native. The player launches the game with the VR runtime already active and the mod brings the XR view up automatically. The documented control scheme uses the right controller as a UI pointer: trigger clicks, while another face action handles context-sensitive interaction/jump/right-click behavior. The architecture is appropriate for a closed Unity IL2CPP title where managed gameplay can be reached through BepInEx/interop assemblies while native OpenXR is supplied beside the plugin. An LLM implementing a similar mod should keep three concerns separate: BepInEx/IL2CPP initialization and method patching, OpenXR session/controller state, and per-game camera/UI/interaction patches. The repository is especially useful as a reminder that the OpenXR loader's physical location and native dependency resolution matter just as much as the managed DLL.",
