    "summary": "Give every physical affordance the same enter/exit/press/release lifecycle and let acknowledged presses hold exclusive hand ownership until release.",
    "details": "PHYSICAL INTERACTION: The public `VRInteractable` contract exposes `Flags`, `OnColliderEnter`, `OnColliderExit`, `OnButtonPress` and `OnButtonRelease`. `InteractionManager` tracks the current intersected object and held object per hand. If `OnButtonPress` returns true, the interaction is acknowledged/owned until release and collider exit is deferred; false allows retry while the button remains held. Flags select left/right/both hands and can reject use while holding another object. `VRInteractor.SnapTo` can temporarily drive the arm target from an authored interaction anchor while keeping the real controller as the physical source.\n\nARCHITECTURE: This converts dozens of game-specific buttons/doors/levers into small adapters around one reusable arbitration layer.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: `Source/Player/VRInteractor.cs`, `Docs/API/README.md`, `Source/Physics/Interactions/*`.",
