    "details": "VEHICLES: `SteeringWheel` creates physical snap points. Grip forces a fist and snaps the visible/IK hand to the selected wheel point while retaining the real tracked controller as the target. `ApplyRotationAtPointTowards` transforms both snap point and target into wheel-local space, flattens Z and measures signed angle around wheel forward; this accumulates pending rotation. `SmoothDampAngle` limits/smooths the wheel within ±480°, with speed affected by number of hands. `GetSteeringInput` maps rotation into `vehicle.steeringInput`; accelerator/brake remain the native Move action Y.\n\nMULTIPLAYER: A channel scoped by vehicle NetworkObjectId replicates wheel state and hand attach/release; receivers validate the sender as current driver and snap the remote VR hand to the same point.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: `Source/Physics/Interactions/Car/SteeringWheel.cs`, `Source/Patches/CarPatches.cs`.",
