    "summary": "A source-available modernization of Subnautica's original VR mode with SteamVR motion controls, laser-pointer UI, quickslot gestures, tracked hands, haptics and vehicle-aware HUD behavior.",
    "details": "SubmersedVR began from the SN1MC source and combines fixes from the Subnautica VR Enhancements project with the authors' own input/UI work. The motion-control layer uses SteamVR/OpenVR and supplies default bindings for Oculus Touch and Valve Index. The right controller drives a laser pointer whose aim direction can vary by equipped tool; bare hands use a different default angle. Quickslots are moved out of the flat HUD and selected with a thumbstick-flick radial interaction inspired by Half-Life: Alyx. Seamoth/exosuit modules use the same interaction vocabulary. The project later added articulated/tracked SteamVR hands and optional game/UI haptics. Release history also documents virtual keyboard work, wrist health/oxygen display experiments, UI scrolling, hand rotation fixes, tool/exosuit aiming fixes and an experimental option to attach the hand reticle to the laser-pointer endpoint. Roomscale was initially absent and recentering was used to handle playspace drift, which is a useful example of a VR retrofit whose tracking origin and player-world origin were not originally designed to move independently. Vehicle HUD is explicitly fixed/static instead of remaining head-following. For an LLM, this is a strong reference for converting a flat inventory/tool HUD into hand/controller-directed VR interactions while leaving the game's underlying inventory/vehicle systems authoritative.",
    "blockers": "SteamVR/OpenVR is the supported runtime path in the source releases; physical driving work has changed across versions and should not be assumed from the feature history.",
    "sourceLinks": "https://github.com/Okabintaro/SubmersedVR",
    "submittedBy": "source-audit",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-05"
