    "summary": "A native Creation Engine 2 VR retrofit that combines a proxy-DLL bootstrap, a shared VR/D3D framework, and Starfield-specific hooks for frame timing, per-eye projection, HMD camera pose, Scaleform HUD viewport handling, gamepad input and weapon state.",
    "details": "Deep source audit of the supplied starfield2vr snapshot: DllMain starts a delayed InitThread, which constructs the shared Framework; the CMake build defaults to a DXGI proxy output (with dinput8/PhysX/inject alternatives) and enables DX12-first hooking plus optional signature scanning. CreationEngineEntry then installs three main engine adapters: CameraManager, RendererModule and InputManager. RendererModule hooks the internal NVIDIA Reflex marker function, the Creation Renderer render-graph frame start, camera constant-buffer updates and the TemporalAA render-pass vtable. Reflex marker 6/0/1 is used as the engine/wait boundary: it records the engine frame index, calls the VR wait/begin path, samples HMD state, runs the overlay and updates the world camera; marker 2 records the render frame and marker 4 the presenter frame. After warm-up, an unexpected mid-frame marker can set skip-next-present to re-phase alternate-frame stereo. The renderer also maintains per-resource past buffers and swaps history resources by render-frame parity, addressing temporal-history/TAA contamination between alternating eyes. CameraManager injects the runtime's current-eye asymmetric frustum into valid NiCamera objects, tracks FOV/near/far values, converts the HMD transform into Havok space, and writes the resulting per-eye head pose into the world camera. It separately hooks FirstPersonState rotation so authored player rotation, optional pawn-control yaw and HMD orientation can be combined, and hooks Scaleform MovieImpl viewport sizing to place/scale HUD and menus differently per eye. InputManager hooks the game's BSPCGamepadDevice poll, updates VR action states, converts them through the framework's XInput-facing semantic state, and feeds an emulated Xbox 360 controller through ViGEm. WeaponModule hooks weapon/object update and equipped-weapon lookup; the supplied code shows an equipped optical-sight adjustment and a debug weapon-node transform path, while the older direct muzzle hook is disabled. HavokModule hooks NiPointerSet and two Havok weapon raycast paths. Memory access is not uniformly signature-driven: ScanHelper supports debug/signature scanning with RTTI vtable discovery, function byte patterns and instruction-relative relocation, but release builds can fall back to static offsets; some weapon hooks in the supplied snapshot still use raw module-relative addresses. The vrframework submodule itself is not populated in the supplied ZIP, so its exact OpenXR/OpenVR runtime and DX12 submission implementation must be treated as external framework context rather than falsely attributed to these Starfield source files. This makes the strongest reusable architecture explicit: proxy/bootstrap -> shared VR/D3D core -> Creation Engine 2 timing/render/camera/input adapters -> version-specific offsets and engine data.",
    "blockers": "Experimental and version-sensitive. The supplied source snapshot does not include the vrframework submodule contents, so framework-level OpenXR/OpenVR submission details require the referenced vrframework repository. Exact Starfield offsets/functions must be re-derived and validated against the target executable; the snapshot mixes signature-capable relocation helpers with static-offset and raw module-relative hooks.",
    "sourceLinks": "https://github.com/mutars/starfield2vr, https://github.com/elliotttate/vrframework",
    "submittedBy": "source-audit",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-05"
