    "summary": "Expose only poses, semantic action state, display/projection data, texture sharing/submission, haptics and device identity to Lua; keep OpenVR and graphics handles entirely native.",
    "details": "ARCHITECTURE: `src/vrmod.cpp` registers a deliberately small `vrmod` Lua table: lifecycle (`Init`/`Shutdown`), action-manifest/action-set configuration, `GetDisplayInfo`, one per-frame `UpdatePosesAndActions`, `GetPoses`, `GetActions`, shared-texture capture/submission, `TriggerHaptic` and tracked-device names. `core/cl_vrmod.lua` loads this with `require(\"vrmod\")` and aliases it to `VRMOD_*`, while all Source-specific camera, viewmodel, locomotion, interaction, UI and networking code remains Lua. The reusable seam is capability-shaped rather than runtime-object-shaped: gameplay never receives `IVRSystem`, action handles or compositor objects.\n\nNATIVE GAMEPLAY AUTHORITY: Native C++ owns XR lifetime and graphics interop; Lua owns game semantics. This makes the runtime module replaceable without rewriting every interaction subsystem.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: native `src/vrmod.cpp`, module `README`; Lua `core/cl_vrmod.lua`, `api/cl_api.lua`, `api/sv_api.lua`.\n\nLIMITATIONS: This supplied native module is OpenVR-specific. The separate gVRMod OpenXR backend already has its own registry case; do not merge their exact native APIs.",
