    "summary": "When the engine does not expose the VR render target handle, arm a one-shot native texture-creation hook immediately before Lua creates the target, capture exactly that allocation, then restore the original function bytes.",
    "details": "RENDERING: `VRMOD_ShareTextureBegin()` patches the platform texture-creation function so the next texture allocation jumps into `CreateTextureHook`. Lua immediately calls `GetRenderTargetEx` from `SetupRenderTargets`; the hook captures that texture/share handle and restores the original bytes on its first invocation. On Windows it intercepts the D3D9 device `CreateTexture` path; on Linux it resolves ToGL/OpenGL entry points and intercepts texture generation. `ShareTextureFinish()` then completes the backend-specific sharing setup.\n\nARCHITECTURE: This is a narrow interception-window methodology for engines where the scripting API can request a render target but cannot expose the native resource needed by an XR compositor. Arming only around the intended allocation is less invasive than permanently hooking every texture creation.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: native `src/vrmod.cpp::{ShareTextureBegin,CreateTextureHook,ShareTextureFinish}`; Lua `core/cl_vrmod.lua::SetupRenderTargets`.\n\nLIMITATIONS: Byte/vtable/entry-point interception is platform/build-sensitive. The method assumes no unrelated texture allocation wins the race between arming the hook and creating the intended render target.",
    "sourceLinks": "https://github.com/Metastruct/vrmod, https://github.com/Abyss-c0re/vrmod-module-master",
