    "details": "RENDERING: Native `GetDisplayInfo` returns raw OpenVR left/right projection matrices plus recommended per-eye dimensions. `utils/cl_rendering.lua::CalculateProjectionParams` extracts X/Y scales and projection-center offsets, derives tangent extents, horizontal FOV and aspect. Lua allocates one target at `2 * RecommendedWidth` by `RecommendedHeight`; `PerformRenderViews` renders left/right into the two halves. `ComputeSubmitBounds` uses the retained projection-center terms to shift/scale each eye's UV rectangle, with Linux V inversion, and `SetSubmitTextureBounds` stores those rectangles for the native compositor submit.\n\nCAMERA / TRACKING: Eye positions still use OpenVR eye-to-head transforms/IPD; the UV correction is specifically a projection compatibility layer.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: native `src/vrmod.cpp::GetDisplayInfo,SetSubmitTextureBounds,SubmitSharedTexture`; Lua `utils/cl_rendering.lua::{CalculateProjectionParams,AdjustFOV,ComputeSubmitBounds}`, `core/cl_vrmod.lua::{ComputeDisplayParams,PerformRenderViews,SetupRenderTargets}`.\n\nLIMITATIONS: This is not a mathematically identical replacement for supplying Source a full asymmetric off-axis projection matrix. It is a practical adaptation to `render.RenderView`'s FOV/aspect interface and should be described that way.",
