    "summary": "Centralize pose/action refresh, tracking conversion, physical-presentation correction, input/network state, camera update, both eye renders and compositor submit under one Source render hook.",
    "details": "FRAME TIMING: `core/cl_vrmod.lua::BindRenderSceneHook` runs: `VRMOD_UpdatePosesAndActions()` → `UpdateTracking()` → `UpdateCollisionsAndWepPos()` → `HandleInput()` → `VRUtilNetUpdateLocalPly()` → `UpdateViewFromEntity()` → `PerformRenderViews()` → `VRMOD_SubmitSharedTexture()` → `VRMod_PostRender`. Native `UpdatePosesAndActions` calls `VRCompositor()->WaitGetPoses` then `VRInput()->UpdateActionState`; the module README states that this call also paces FPS to headset refresh. `PerformRenderViews` issues two Source `render.RenderView` calls into one target.\n\nARCHITECTURE: One hook owns the XR-facing frame ordering, which prevents unrelated Think/UI/network code from independently sampling tracking at inconsistent times.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: Lua `core/cl_vrmod.lua::{BindRenderSceneHook,PerformRenderViews,UpdateTracking}`; native `src/vrmod.cpp::UpdatePosesAndActions`.\n\nLIMITATIONS: There is no source-established freeze of Source simulation, random render state or once-per-frame side effects between the left and right `RenderView` calls. Do not describe this as deterministic stereo replay.",
    "sourceLinks": "https://github.com/Metastruct/vrmod, https://github.com/Abyss-c0re/vrmod-module-master",
    "submittedBy": "source-audit",
