    "details": "CAMERA / TRACKING: Native `GetPoses` maps OpenVR position to Source/GMod as `(-Z,-X,+Y)` and applies the same axis remap to linear velocity; angular velocity is remapped and converted rad/s→deg/s. Pose actions are requested with `GetPoseActionDataRelativeToNow(..., TrackingUniverseStanding, 0, ...)`. Lua `UpdateTracking` multiplies position/velocity by `g_VR.scale`, rotates them by `g_VR.originAngle`, translates through `g_VR.origin`, applies per-controller calibration offsets, optional smoothing and stores canonical world poses in `g_VR.tracking`.\n\nARCHITECTURE: World origin/rotation/scale become first-class state. Roomscale, weapons, UI, vehicles and networking can all reference the same converted pose contract.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: native `src/vrmod.cpp::GetPoses`; Lua `core/cl_vrmod.lua::UpdateTracking`, `api/cl_api.lua`.\n\nLIMITATIONS: `TrackingUniverseStanding` is hard-coded in the native pose-action query. The addon then handles seated/artificial offsets at the Lua/world layer.",
