    "details": "INPUT: `cl_steamvr_bindings.lua` defines the pose/skeleton/haptic actions and action sets. Native `SetActionManifest` parses the action manifest and resolves handles; `SetActiveActionSets` caches selected action-set handles; `GetActions` returns analog values plus only-changed booleans in a second table. `cl_input.lua` consumes those edge changes to execute Source-style press/release commands such as `+attack/-attack`, `+attack2/-attack2`, `+reload/-reload`, jump/duck, flashlight and menu actions. Vehicle enter/exit changes the active action set to `/actions/driving` or main gameplay.\n\nNATIVE GAMEPLAY AUTHORITY: Weapons, movement and addons that already react to Source commands continue to work; XR bindings do not replace their gameplay state machines.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: native `src/vrmod.cpp::{SetActionManifest,SetActiveActionSets,GetActions}`; Lua `input/cl_steamvr_bindings.lua`, `input/cl_input.lua`.\n\nLIMITATIONS: This is action-manifest/controller-input abstraction, not hand-tracking gesture recognition by itself.",
