    "details": "BODY / IK: `player/cl_character.lua::CharacterInit` resolves ValveBiped clavicle/upper-arm/forearm/hand bones and measures segment lengths from the actual model. `UpdateIK::ProcessArm` takes the network/local tracked hand target, points the clavicle part-way toward the target, builds the shoulder→hand vector, clamps the reach to the measured arm chain, and uses law-of-cosines angles (`acos`) to solve upper-arm and elbow bend. Additional body-yaw/hand-height policy biases roll. Wrist orientation is decomposed from the target hand angle; where a ValveBiped ulna/wrist bone exists, `LerpAngle(0.5, forearm, wrist)` shares twist instead of dumping it all into one joint.\n\nARCHITECTURE: The solver works for local and remote VR players because it consumes the normalized per-player frame rather than OpenVR devices directly.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: `player/cl_character.lua::{CharacterInit,UpdateIK,ProcessArm}`.\n\nLIMITATIONS: This is heuristic two-bone avatar IK, not an anatomically constrained full-body solver; tracked waist/feet are not fed into it.",
