    "summary": "When client visual hands cannot participate in server VPhysics, create separate per-hand physics entities and servo them toward the server's predicted VR poses.",
    "details": "PHYSICAL INTERACTION: `physics/sv_physhands.lua` creates hidden `base_anim` entities for each VR hand, marks them with `NWBool(\"isVRHand\", true)`, initializes sphere physics, and can replace the right-hand shape with weapon-derived box geometry after weapon changes. Every `PlayerTick`, each proxy is driven toward `vrmod.GetLeft/RightHandPos/Ang(ply)` plus the configured hand-forward offset using `PhysicsObject:ComputeShadowControl`. Proxies are disabled while the player is in a vehicle and are created/removed across VR start, spawn, death, exit, cleanup and disconnect.\n\nARCHITECTURE: Visual IK hands, client wall-pushout hands and server physics hands are intentionally different objects with different authority responsibilities.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: `physics/sv_physhands.lua`; server pose API in `api/sv_api.lua`; geometry in `utils/sh_collisions.lua`.\n\nLIMITATIONS: Shadow-controlled proxies approximate tracked motion; they are not the same rigid body as the user's controller and can lag/network-predict independently of local visuals.",
