    "summary": "Let the client detect responsive swing/contact candidates, but never trust its claimed hit: send geometry, re-evaluate tracked speed and trace on the server, then build authoritative `DamageInfo`.",
    "details": "MELEE: On `VRMod_Tracking`, `combat/sh_combat.lua` precomputes hand/weapon geometry. Hand velocity is explicitly measured relative to HMD (`GetLeft/RightHandVelocityRelative`) so player/world locomotion is less likely to count as a swing. After the configured speed threshold is exceeded, the client traces `TraceBoxOrSphere` using model-derived radius/reach/box/angles and sends the proposed geometry/impact class. The server re-derives HMD-relative swing speed from `api/sv_api.lua`, repeats `TraceBoxOrSphere` with server filtering, applies cooldown, then creates `DamageInfo`, damage type/position/force, sound/decal and `VRMod_MeleeHit` extension callbacks. Damage is `base * min(5, 1+swingSpeed*speedScale) * impactMultiplier`.\n\nNATIVE GAMEPLAY AUTHORITY: Entity damage occurs only after server trace validation.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: `combat/sh_combat.lua`; `utils/sh_collisions.lua::{TraceBoxOrSphere,GetWeaponMeleeParams}`; `api/sv_api.lua` relative velocity getters.\n\nLIMITATIONS: Contact is a current-pose box/sphere trace rather than a continuous historical sweep. The code reads target velocity but currently sets `relativeSpeed = swingSpeed`; target motion is not actually subtracted from the damage-speed term.",
