    "summary": "Spatialize legacy UI without rewriting widgets: render the real panel offscreen, show it as a 3D2D quad, ray-intersect the plane, then feed the hit into Garry’s Mod’s existing cursor and mouse handlers.",
    "details": "UI: `ui/cl_ui.lua` manually paints VGUI panels into render targets and draws them with `cam.Start3D2D` at world/tracking/left-hand-relative poses. The right controller supplies the pointer ray. Ray-plane intersection and local basis conversion yield panel pixel coordinates; the nearest active menu receives focus and the addon drives `gui.EnableScreenClicker`, `input.SetCursorPos`, `gui.InternalMousePressed` and `gui.InternalMouseReleased`. The panel's normal VGUI callbacks/state remain intact.\n\nARCHITECTURE: UI visual placement and input adaptation are separate from widget implementation, making existing addon menus reusable.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: `ui/cl_ui.lua`; `api/cl_api.lua` menu API.\n\nLIMITATIONS: Native cursor injection means other systems fighting over the desktop cursor can still conflict; focus arbitration is required when multiple VR panels overlap.",
