    "details": "HAPTICS: Native `TriggerHaptic(actionName, delay, duration, frequency, amplitude)` resolves the named action created from the action manifest and calls `IVRInput::TriggerHapticVibrationAction`. The supplied bindings include left/right haptic output actions. This establishes a reusable runtime endpoint and handed action routing.\n\nARCHITECTURE: A haptic output API is useful even before semantic event mapping exists because gameplay addons can target it without touching OpenVR handles.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: native `src/vrmod.cpp::TriggerHaptic`; action definitions in `input/cl_steamvr_bindings.lua`/manifest setup.\n\nLIMITATIONS: Searching the supplied Metastruct Lua source finds no call site to `VRMOD_TriggerHaptic`/native `TriggerHaptic`. Do not claim active weapon, melee, UI or damage haptics from this snapshot.",
