    "details": "ARCHITECTURE: `api/cl_api.lua` exposes local/remote HMD and hand poses, raw and HMD-relative velocity/angular velocity, smoothed visual hand-pose overrides, open/closed finger-pose getters/setters, extracting hand/finger poses from models, input queries, VR menu render/cursor helpers, viewmodel offset/muzzle/laser configuration, locomotion option registration, origin get/set, eye positions and tracked-device names. `api/sv_api.lua` exposes server world HMD/hand pose and derived velocity/angular velocity, relative velocity, held entities and interaction helpers based on the predicted server pose cache.\n\nARCHITECTURE: The API is semantic and game-facing. Addons can implement new SWEPs/interactions without depending on `IVRSystem`, Lua-module internals or the exact tracking network format.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: `api/cl_api.lua`, `api/sv_api.lua`, `api/sh_api.lua` plus public VRMod hook aliases.\n\nLIMITATIONS: Some API calls expose current implementation policy (for example predicted server poses); addon code should prefer semantic getters over reaching into the backing cache/network tables.",
