    "summary": "A classic DXGI proxy VR mod valuable for studying SDK-call redirection in a closed game: the mod forwards legacy Oculus requests into a modern runtime and translates/fixes them without game source access.",
    "details": "MotherVR installs as a `dxgi.dll` beside Alien: Isolation and exposes VR configuration in-game. Its historical architecture is notable because Alien: Isolation embedded an obsolete Oculus SDK directly in the executable; the mod therefore intercepted SDK calls and redirected them into replacement code instead of patching an engine source tree. Release documentation also shows an optional `openvr_api.dll` SteamVR path and deliberate suppression of intro/loading frames where the game's eye-glued video path was unsuitable for VR. The reusable pattern is an API-boundary compatibility shim: intercept a stable call family, translate parameters/state into a current runtime, and preserve the game's expected contract.",
