    "summary": "A Source-engine D3D9/OpenVR retrofit whose source exposes the full path from tracked poses and asymmetric eye projections through engine render targets, compositor submission and controller-driven VGUI interaction.",
    "details": "The repository builds an x86 d3d9.dll and is derived from the L4D2VR/Source SDK lineage. Its implementation is useful because rendering, engine access, input and UI are separate concerns: OpenVR provides poses and eye projection data; Source's MaterialSystem supplies per-eye render targets; the mod submits those textures independently to the OpenVR compositor; and controller poses are converted into Source coordinate conventions before gameplay commands are emitted. The portal gun and grabbable-object interactions therefore sit on top of a reusable tracked-controller layer rather than owning the compositor themselves. The HUD/menu path also demonstrates a practical bridge between VR and legacy flatscreen UI: controller-tip rays are converted into VGUI cursor coordinates, with mouse/keyboard or wheel events forwarded into the existing interface. The project uses signature scanning instead of assuming fixed absolute addresses, which is important for Source-engine builds that shift between patches. This is a strong reference for preserving the game's native action vocabulary (+attack, +attack2, +jump, +duck, +use, +reload, inventory commands) while replacing only the input source.",
    "blockers": "The implementation is x86/D3D9-specific and its README still lists in-game UI/pause-menu and full roomscale issues. It is a native hook retrofit, not a portable Source SDK VR framework.",
