    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE. `idPlayer::CalculateViewWeaponPosVR` samples the selected controller, applies a configurable weapon-pitch calibration, converts the controller pose through body yaw/head displacement into world space, keeps special-case game items such as the PDA/Artifact/SoulCube in their intended presentation path, and calls `SetHandIKPos`. `SetHandIKPos` does not simply pin the wrist to the controller. It reads the active weapon's `weaponHandAttacher` joint for the current animation frame, subtracts its stored default position to obtain an animation delta, adds that delta to the controller-driven target, converts the target into player-model local space, compensates the hand's own weapon-attacher-to-wrist offset and per-weapon correction axis, then writes the arm IK hand joint with `JOINTMOD_WORLD_OVERRIDE`. `idIK_Reach` reads shoulder/elbow/hand/wrist joints, solves a two-bone arm, chooses an elbow bend direction from the original rig, and uses controller roll to distribute constrained forearm/wrist twist. Reusable pattern: controller pose defines physical intent; weapon animation supplies local attachment deltas; skeletal IK reconciles the body to both. This avoids choosing between completely rigid VR weapons and completely authored flat-screen hand animation.",
