    "details": "Full source audit of the sd805/l4d2vr tree (dllmain, game, hooks, vr, offsets, sigscanner). The mod loads as a d3d9.dll (DXVK proxy) and requires -insecure. Game initialization resolves Source interfaces with retry + cache; every hook target is signature-scanned and fails closed. dRenderView issues two independent CViewSetups (left/right eye origins from HMD + eye-to-head + IPD, shared HMD angles) into named MaterialSystem render targets, then submits the DXVK Vulkan shared textures to the OpenVR compositor with per-eye texture bounds derived from GetProjectionRaw. HUD is intercepted by call-sequence detection (IsSplitScreen -> PrePushRenderTarget -> PushRenderTargetAndViewport) and redirected to a dedicated overlay. Weapons: FireTerrorBullets (client+server) replace origin/angles with the right-controller absolute pose. Melee: ProcessUsercmds reconstructs a continuous arc from previous->current controller angle (10 traces around the swing pivot) and calls native TestMeleeSwingCollisionServer; EyePosition is overridden during the swing. Multiplayer: WriteUsercmd packs controller pose into existing CUserCmd fields (tick_count sign, command_number encoding, viewangles packing, upmove, mousedx/y) and recalculates the verified checksum; ReadUsercmd decodes it on the server into a per-player VR state array. Roomscale uses an explicit camera anchor + height offset + wall-clip TraceRay, disabled while the thumbstick is active. OpenVR Input actions are mapped to ClientCmd for maximum compatibility. Arms model is optionally hidden via DrawModelExecute material override.",
