    "details": "Keep XR reference space, player/body space, camera/view space and object/attachment space distinct. Convert controller/HMD poses from the runtime reference space into a stable player tracking anchor, then derive hand, head, weapon and IK targets in the appropriate local frame. For a first-person weapon, use controller pose -> tracking anchor -> weapon grip/socket frame -> weapon orientation; for body IK use HMD/controller pose -> avatar-local targets -> limb solve. Recenter should move the tracking anchor or calibration offset, not rewrite every child transform. Solve hands in the avatar or shoulder frame after removing head/tracking-anchor motion so head movement does not contaminate arm orientation. OpenXR provides VIEW, LOCAL and STAGE-style reference spaces plus action spaces; use VIEW for view-relative targeting/reticles and a world-locked space for player/world interaction.",
