    "summary": "A hardware-neutral input layer that maps tracked poses, buttons, axes and haptics into semantic actions before game-specific code consumes them.",
    "details": "Do not make gameplay code depend directly on controller vendor paths or physical device indices. Define semantic actions such as Move, Turn, Grab, PrimaryAttack, SecondaryAttack, Reload, Use, Jump, MenuSelect and Recenter. Bind them to OpenXR interaction-profile paths or an OpenVR action manifest, then expose normalized button/axis/pose state to the game layer. Pose inputs should be separate from digital actions: a grip or aim pose is a transform source, while Grab or Fire is an action state. Handedness becomes a logical role assignment rather than a hardware assumption. The same semantic state can feed native VR gameplay, legacy keyboard/gamepad emulation or a hybrid bridge. OpenXR explicitly separates application actions from physical trigger/thumbstick/button paths and groups them into action sets.",
