    "details": "The Two Forks VR codebase is useful as a broad Unity pattern because the repository separates the runtime mod from its patcher and Unity helper tooling. The practical lesson is to create a narrow VR adapter layer: initialize the XR runtime, replace or augment the player camera, translate controller poses into the game’s interaction vocabulary, then leave ordinary Firewatch gameplay and UI code intact. For vibe-coded projects, this suggests a stable split between (1) bootstrap/config, (2) camera/pose ownership, (3) controller-to-game input translation, and (4) game-specific patches. The mod also demonstrates that comfort features should live beside the VR rig rather than inside individual gameplay systems, so snap/smooth turning and height/scale adjustments can be changed without rewriting interaction code. When adapting the pattern to another Unity title, first identify the authoritative camera and player-input components, then make VR own only those seams; do not duplicate the game’s entire locomotion or interaction state machine unless necessary.",
