    "details": "The Dark Mod is useful because the source tree exposes renderer, game, framework, UI and system layers rather than a single opaque plugin. Its VR implementation is deliberately conservative: the current project supports a seated keyboard/mouse or gamepad experience rather than pretending roomscale and tracked-hand interaction are solved. The broad implementation lesson is important: make VR an alternate presentation/input mode, not an assumption baked into every gameplay system. Keep the renderer responsible for stereo/OpenXR presentation, keep the input layer responsible for translating XR state into actions, and allow gameplay to remain agnostic about whether an action came from a mouse, gamepad or controller. For a new mod, this makes incremental development much easier: first get stereo and head pose correct, then map existing actions, then add physical interactions only where the game has a meaningful world-space object model. It also gives you a safe fallback mode when individual VR systems are incomplete.",
