    "details": "MegabonkVR is unusually useful for broad implementation because the README documents the entire bootstrap chain. The plugin first installs configuration and native-library resolution, then defers engine calls until a MonoBehaviour Update because doing them inside the BepInEx Load phase caused native crashes. A hand-rolled OpenXR bootstrap loads UnityOpenXR, initializes the session, discovers display/input subsystems, and starts the session; the VR camera then follows the game camera position/yaw while applying full HMD pose locally. Crucially, the original Camera.main remains active for game logic and the desktop mirror, while the VR child camera becomes the headset view. This is a strong general pattern for Unity games where destroying/replacing the original camera would break gameplay. The UI solution is equally reusable: capture existing screen-space canvases with an orthographic camera into a RenderTexture, then display that texture on a world-space panel. The project also documents IL2CPP-specific landmines, including deferred initialization, non-generic interop, DllImport resolution, and surviving InputTracking APIs. For vibe coding, the transferable recipe is: bootstrap XR late, preserve the original camera contract, create a dedicated VR rig, bridge UI through a controlled render target, and isolate IL2CPP reflection/interop behind helper functions.",
    "blockers": "The project targets one Unity 2023 IL2CPP build and deliberately uses MultiPass because that particular build lacked stereo-instanced shader variants; another Unity title may need a different render mode.",
