    "title": "#DRIVE Rally — UUVR 0.4.0 Unity 6 stereo/head-tracked VR retrofit",
    "game": "#DRIVE Rally",
    "engineFamily": "Unity 6 (6000.0.73f1 / 6000.0.73.10577579 in supplied runtime log)",
    "renderAPI": "Unity XR backend; supplied package includes both Unity OpenXR and XRSDK OpenVR backends; exact active graphics API is not identified in the supplied log",
    "injectionMethod": "BepInEx 5 x64 + UUVR 0.4.0 managed plugin/preloader patching, with UUVR XR Management and OpenXR/OpenVR backend plugins",
    "platform": "PC VR; OpenXR or OpenVR/SteamVR",
    "status": "proven",
    "features": [],
    "summary": "A clean example of using the universal Unity VR layer on #DRIVE Rally rather than building a game-specific VR plugin. The supplied package contains UUVR 0.4.0, its BepInEx patcher, OpenXR/OpenVR backends and the generated configuration/log from a successful launch under Unity 6; public community evidence also reports the game working essentially out of the box with UUVR, while noting desktop-rendered menu elements.",
    "details": "The supplied archive is a complete UUVR/BepInEx installation rather than a game-specific source mod. BepInEx 5.4.23.5 identifies the executable as DRIVERally, reports Unity 6000.0.73.10577579 / 6000.0.73f1, detects x64 Windows, loads the Uuvr.Patcher, then loads UUVR 0.4.0 as the sole runtime plugin. The patcher copies UnityOpenXR and XRSDKOpenVR subsystem manifests plus x64 OpenXR/OpenVR native libraries into the game's Data/Plugins tree, so both XR paths are packaged even though the config selects OpenXR by default.\n\nVR / CAMERA LAYER: raicuparta.uuvr-modern.cfg sets Preferred VR API=OpenXr and Camera Tracking Mode=RelativeTransform. The same config exposes horizon alignment, tracked-camera position offsets, optional camera-depth override, physics-rate synchronization, and relative-camera SetStereoView behavior. The UUVR binary string surface confirms dedicated Uuvr.VrCamera, VrCameraManager, camera tracking, stereo target-eye handling, XR device abstractions, and VR UI management. This is therefore a general Unity camera/stereo retrofit rather than a custom #DRIVE Rally renderer.\n\nUI / COMPATIBILITY LAYER: the supplied default profile leaves UI Patch Mode=None, Screen-space UI Elements to Patch=None and Preferred UI Plane Render Mode=InWorld. The archive log records a successful UUVR patch/install pass and a normal BepInEx chainloader startup. It also records Rewired warnings about missing UICancel / Change Quality actions and Rewired initialization, but those are not evidence that the VR camera itself failed. Public #DRIVE Rally community reports independently describe UUVR as working 'pretty much out of the box' / 'perfectly fine in VR', with some menus rendering to the desktop instead of the headset; the developer linked a UUVR preview.\n\nWHAT IS NOT PRESENT: there is no game-specific C# plugin, Lua profile, native renderer hook, custom vehicle interaction layer, motion-controller driving system, wheel implementation, or hand/gesture implementation in the supplied archive. UUVR's general binary contains camera/stereo/UI infrastructure, but the supplied DRIVERally package does not provide evidence for tagging handsControls, weaponAiming, meleeCombat, bodyIK, physicalInteraction or gestureInteraction. The archive also does not identify the active D3D11/D3D12/Vulkan graphics backend, so the renderAPI field intentionally stays at the Unity XR abstraction level.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION LESSON: this is a useful baseline for an LLM because it demonstrates the minimum viable path for a Unity 6 game that already works with UUVR: BepInEx preloader/chainloader -> UUVR camera/stereo layer -> selectable OpenXR/OpenVR backend. Game-specific behavior should only be added after verifying a real need; do not infer custom input, wheel, cockpit, or interaction hooks from the existence of the generic XR binaries.",
    "blockers": "The supplied artifact is a universal UUVR package, not a source-level #DRIVE Rally VR mod. Some UI remains desktop-oriented according to public user/developer reports, and the package contains no game-specific wheel/controller interaction implementation. The active graphics API is not established by the supplied log.",
    "sourceLinks": "https://github.com/Raicuparta/uuvr ; https://store.steampowered.com/app/2494780/DRIVE_Rally/",
    "submittedBy": "binary-audit",
