    "details": "FRAME TIMING: `XrSessionGlobals::GetBestTime` prefers the next `predictedDisplayTime` from `xrWaitFrame`, falling back to the latest session-state event time before the first frame. `GetCachedViews(space)` runs `xrLocateViews` once per space/time and stores the result in a mutex-protected map. `WaitForTrackingData` clears that cache at the new frame boundary. `XrHMD::GetProjection*` and `GetEyeToHeadTransform` therefore consume a coherent view sample rather than independently locating eyes at slightly different times.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION USE: In an API façade with many getters, cache canonical runtime queries at the lifecycle boundary and derive all public representations from that snapshot.\n\nSOURCE AUDIT FILES: `OpenOVR/Misc/xrutil.cpp`, `DrvOpenXR/XrHMD.cpp`, `XrBackend.cpp`.",
