    "summary": "Keep spatial insertion eligibility, magazine ownership and native ammo state as distinct concerns.",
    "details": "WEAPON RELOAD / PHYSICAL INTERACTION — VERIFIED PAK EVIDENCE: BP_VRMagazine records InRange, InReloadComp, Aligned, Latched, MagFitsGun, IsBeingHeld, HasJustBeenDetached, AttachedToGun, MagIndex and AmmoState. Its begin/end overlap delegate names are serialized alongside Mag Attach and MagAttached. BP_VRReloadComp supplies ReloadCapsule, ReloadLatch and Enable Collision With Delay. This is substantially richer than a single overlap-to-reload flag.\n\nWEAPON RELOAD / PHYSICAL INTERACTION — PORTABLE IMPLEMENTATION RECIPE: For another port, use overlap to nominate a candidate magwell, item/ammo identity to validate compatibility, alignment and travel to validate insertion, and a single commit step to invoke the native reload/ammo-transfer API. Transfer ownership only after successful commit. Keep an ejected/recently-detached state so an item still intersecting its former magwell cannot immediately reinsert. Route the visible magazine and hand pose from the same accepted state.\n\nWEAPON RELOAD / PHYSICAL INTERACTION — VALIDATION: Check wrong magazine type, repeated overlap notifications, partial insertion, ejection while overlapping, and native reload rejection. Inventory plus loaded ammo should conserve the expected total. This transaction ordering is a recommended adaptation, not a reconstructed call graph.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Ready or Not VRO, supplied `pakchunk98-VR_OR_NOT_P.pak`; cooked-package metadata audit, 2026-09-07. References below were checked as length-prefixed serialized strings, including their byte offsets in the extracted .uasset. They establish symbols, data fields and references; the proposed recipe is not a bytecode decompilation.\n\nSOURCE ASSETS: `/Game/VR_OR_NOT/Assets/GunRelated/BP_VRMagazine`: `MagFitsGun` (string offset 0x1837), `HasJustBeenDetached` (string offset 0x12DB), `AmmoState` (string offset 0x2A8), `MagAttached` (string offset 0x17D2). `/Game/VR_OR_NOT/Assets/GunRelated/BP_VRReloadComp`: `ReloadCapsule` (string offset 0xA97), `ReloadLatch` (string offset 0xAC1), `Enable Collision With Delay` (string offset 0x683).",
