    "details": "ARM IK / HANDS / COORDINATE SPACES — VERIFIED PAK EVIDENCE: Hands_RON_Anim contains TwoBoneIK exposed-input evaluator names, AnimNode_TwoBoneIK, AnimNode_Fabrik, ModifyBone, local/component conversion nodes, JointTargetLocationSpace, EffectorLocationSpace, Correction_MCL/MCR and separate left/right hand/forearm/shoulder bone names. It references dummy hands, controller actors and magazine/two-hand targets.\n\nARM IK / HANDS / COORDINATE SPACES — PORTABLE IMPLEMENTATION RECIPE: For an implementation, resolve a target from current ownership: free hand, weapon grip, support grip or mechanism. Convert the world target into skeletal-component space before solving, or select world space consistently if the engine solver supports it. Supply elbow hints and define separately whether wrist rotation comes from the controller or authored object anchor. Blend target changes without changing the underlying tracked pose. Apply finger pose as its own state so touching a trigger need not perturb the arm solution.\n\nARM IK / HANDS / COORDINATE SPACES — VALIDATION: Rotate the avatar root, change player height, reach across the body and switch between free and supported grip. Watch for double transforms, elbow flips and wrist roll discontinuities. Metadata proves the solver types and available target/space fields; it does not determine exact active graph wiring or numeric defaults.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Ready or Not VRO, supplied `pakchunk98-VR_OR_NOT_P.pak`; cooked-package metadata audit, 2026-09-07. References below were checked as length-prefixed serialized strings, including their byte offsets in the extracted .uasset. They establish symbols, data fields and references; the proposed recipe is not a bytecode decompilation.\n\nSOURCE ASSETS: `/Game/VR_OR_NOT/Character_RON/Hands_RON_Anim`: `AnimNode_TwoBoneIK` (string offset 0x1A18), `AnimNode_Fabrik` (string offset 0x192C), `JointTargetLocationSpace` (string offset 0xEEE), `EffectorLocationSpace` (string offset 0x96C), `Correction_MCL` (string offset 0x89B).",
