    "summary": "Separate temporal reconstruction history per eye; verified against SPT-VR 1.3.0.",
    "details": "RENDERING / FRAME TIMING: DLSSPatches intercepts SSAAImpl.TryRenderDLSS and creates two DLSSWrapper instances. CopyDepthMotion and OnRenderImage select a wrapper with (int)camera.stereoActiveEye % 2; quality, motion-vector scale, sharpness and debug settings are propagated to both. OnDestroy destroys both histories. FSRPatches similarly intercepts TryRenderFSR2/TryRenderFSR3 with stereo wrappers and supplies depth/motion/reactive resources, shared jitter and output dimensions. VRJitterHelper indexes a Halton(2,3) sequence by Time.frameCount so both eyes use the same sample index. Sample count changes with render scale. VRJitterComponent.OnPreRender saves the projection, stores nonJitteredProjectionMatrix and adds pixel-space jitter to m02/m12 using scaled XR eye dimensions; OnPostRender restores the saved projection. Rendering.cs replaces desktop resolution queries with XRSettings.eyeTextureWidth/Height.\n\nRENDERING / FRAME TIMING IMPLEMENTATION USE: Partition temporal history by eye while sharing frame-level sample time/index. Keep render resolution, depth, motion vectors, jitter and reconstruction output in matching units. Reset histories on lifecycle changes. Verify stereoActiveEye behavior in the actual active render mode: an enum modulo operation is source behavior, not proof of correct eye dispatch in every SPI callback. This is temporal reconstruction, not evidence of frame generation.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Supplied `SPT-VR-1.3.0.zip`, C# source audit dated 2026-09-07. Files: `Patches/Upscalers/DLSSPatches.cs`, `Patches/Upscalers/FSRPatches.cs`, `Patches/Upscalers/VRJitterComponent.cs`, `Patches/Visuals/Rendering.cs`. The implementation paragraph describes recovered code; adaptation and validation guidance is identified separately.",
