    "details": "RENDERING: ImpostorCullingPatches.WidenImpostorCullFrustum replaces the tree-impostor plane calculation. It multiplies projection.m00 by 0.9 before composing projection*worldToCameraMatrix, computes six planes and packs them for the culling shader. It does not alter the billboard orientation/size inputs. GPUInstancerPatches loads the VR compute shader and resolves its kernel IDs, adjusts its own culling matrix and optionally supplies a right-eye projection for both-eye occlusion testing. Its motion-vector clear patch writes identity _PreviousVP/_NonJitteredVP matrices as a compatibility workaround. The older blanket disable-all-culling patch is commented out. PostProcessing.FixPostProcessing actively destroys the legacy PostProcessLayer; the alternative force-stereo-context patch is also commented out.\n\nRENDERING IMPLEMENTATION USE: Inspect independent visibility producers such as grass and impostors; a correct main camera does not repair every culling system. Widen projection before view composition, leaving presentation matrices untouched. The 0.9 widening is a heuristic, not an exact union of asymmetric eye frusta. Validate both eye edges, head rotation and render cost. Distinguish active fixes from commented experiments.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Supplied `SPT-VR-1.3.0.zip`, C# source audit dated 2026-09-07. Files: `Patches/Visuals/ImpostorCullingPatches.cs`, `Patches/Visuals/GPUInstancerPatches.cs`, `Patches/Visuals/PostProcessing.cs`. The implementation paragraph describes recovered code; adaptation and validation guidance is identified separately.",
