    "featuresAudited": true,
    "summary": "Preserve orientation when engaging the support hand; verified against SPT-VR 1.3.0.",
    "details": "WEAPON / HANDS / ARM IK: VRPlayerManager.UpdateRightHand forms a long-gun two-hand orientation with LookRotation(leftHand.position-rightHand.position, rightHand.up). On engagement it saves the original primary-hand local rotation, temporarily applies the new two-hand orientation, and stores inverse(newLocalRotation)*initialLocalRotation. Subsequent frames apply the live two-hand rotation and multiply by that stored correction, preserving the entry orientation. Engagement disables the independent offhand LimbIK target and restores the native weapon hand marker. Pistol support uses a separate branch. Scoped breath-hold and general aim smoothing have separate controls. HandsPositioner copies the processed rawRightHand transform to the weapon-holder parent, while per-weapon holder offsets align the existing weapon root. This is a tracked transform adapter around native weapon objects; the audited path does not introduce a replacement ballistic simulation.\n\nWEAPON / HANDS / ARM IK IMPLEMENTATION USE: Capture the primary grip alignment when support begins; apply subsequent two-hand direction changes relative to that alignment. Transfer offhand target ownership with grip state. Test repeated grip/release, handedness and nearly coincident hands; add degeneracy handling when adapting the LookRotation construction. Retain native firing actions and inspect muzzle orientation on the target game.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Supplied `SPT-VR-1.3.0.zip`, C# source audit dated 2026-09-07. Files: `Source/Player/VRManager/VRPlayerManager.cs`, `HandsPositioner.cs`, `Source/Weapons/WeaponHolderOffsets.cs`, `Patches/Core/Player/WeaponPatches.cs`. The implementation paragraph describes recovered code; adaptation and validation guidance is identified separately.",
