    "summary": "Scope-local twist drives persistent optical zoom; verified against SPT-VR 1.3.0.",
    "details": "WEAPON / PHYSICAL INTERACTION / HAPTICS: VROpticController.BeginPhysicalZoom records the initial FOV, derives tracking-to-world rotation from worldHandRot*inverse(localHandRot), transforms the hand-up vector into scope space and records atan2(x,y). TickPhysicalZoom rebuilds world hand rotation from raw tracking, reexpresses it in the current scope frame and uses DeltaAngle against the engagement angle. Smooth scopes clamp travel to 80 degrees, interpolate reciprocal FOV toward the selected limit, then apply a mechanical catch and SmoothDamp with 0.04 seconds. Discrete scopes toggle past 20 degrees and rearm below 10 degrees. Both physical and joystick paths update the native zoom-handler fields and persist the chosen value; detents trigger haptics. A named EOTech HHS scope has a specific bypass.\n\nWEAPON / PHYSICAL INTERACTION / HAPTICS IMPLEMENTATION USE: Measure hand rotation relative to the manipulated optic rather than world yaw. Share one zoom state between physical and joystick controls and write it back to the native handler on completion. Preserve separate visual dial pose, optical output and grip state. Test moving the whole gun while gripping the dial, release/regrip, detent rearming and native scope switching.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Supplied `SPT-VR-1.3.0.zip`, C# source audit dated 2026-09-07. Files: `Source/Weapons/VROpticController.cs`, `Configs/scopes.json`. The implementation paragraph describes recovered code; adaptation and validation guidance is identified separately.",
