    "featuresAudited": true,
    "summary": "Absorb animation stance steps without lagging physical crouch; verified against SPT-VR 1.3.0.",
    "details": "ARM IK / CAMERA TRACKING / LOCOMOTION: InitVRPatches captures existing FinalIK LimbIK components on the local collarbones and configures forearm twist relaxation; it filters other players and bot setup. IKPatches replaces local HeightInterpolation with a render-body-only transient correction: stanceY is ribcage world Y minus animated-body-root world Y, then offset=smoothedStanceY-stanceY clamped to +/-0.2. It uses SmoothDamp at 0.12 seconds, switches to 0.04 seconds when physical HMD vertical speed exceeds 0.12 m/s, and snaps for a large stance discontinuity. InstantBodyPoseLevel assigns SmoothedPoseLevel=PoseLevel_1 so the body animation follows physical crouch. Shoulder placement uses head position, pitch-adjusted neck offset, body yaw and calibrated height; the final shoulder Y can be pinned to the head-derived target. DynamicElbowPositioner derives outward bend hints from wrist twist and freezes them at neutral during run-animation-disabled sprinting.\n\nARM IK / CAMERA TRACKING / LOCOMOTION IMPLEMENTATION USE: Identify whether jitter comes from the controller, shoulder root or native stance animation before smoothing anything. Apply a decaying correction only to the rendered body and keep physical tracking responsive. Test idle/walk boundaries, fast physical crouch and sprint. The source explicitly notes that bypassing SmoothPoseLevel also skips its native stance-change stamina drain; preserve that side effect when adapting.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Supplied `SPT-VR-1.3.0.zip`, C# source audit dated 2026-09-07. Files: `Patches/Core/VR/InitVRPatches.cs`, `Patches/Core/Player/IKPatches.cs`, `Source/Player/Body/DynamicElbowPositioner.cs`. The implementation paragraph describes recovered code; adaptation and validation guidance is identified separately.",
