    "summary": "Velocity hysteresis opens the native knife collision window; verified against SPT-VR 1.3.0.",
    "details": "MELEE / HANDS / MULTIPLAYER: VRMeleeController.ManageKnifeCollider runs after local Player.LateUpdate. It reads the dominant controller velocity directly from SteamVR and rotates it through vrOffsetter. Above 4 m/s it enables the native knife collider, selects Slash, copies the weapon template reach, binds the native method_6 hit handler, calls OnFire and charges native melee stamina. While speed remains above 1 m/s it calls ManualUpdate and updates hit direction from collider-position changes. Below 1 m/s it disables the collider and calls OnFireEnd. SyncMeleeSurfaceHit sends only non-BodyPartCollider ballistic-surface hits to FIKA, because player/AI damage already uses the normal path.\n\nMELEE / HANDS / MULTIPLAYER IMPLEMENTATION USE: Use separate activation and rearm thresholds around the existing game collision/damage mechanism. Read physical velocity in tracking space so player locomotion does not automatically count as a hand swing. Synchronize missing presentation effects without duplicating authoritative damage. The inspected source activates Slash; it does not classify a separate stab gesture or define the internal sweep algorithm of the native collider.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Supplied `SPT-VR-1.3.0.zip`, C# source audit dated 2026-09-07. Files: `Patches/Core/VR/VRMeleeController.cs`, `Source/Controls/ControllerVelocity.cs`, `FikaSync/MeleeHitApply.cs`. The implementation paragraph describes recovered code; adaptation and validation guidance is identified separately.",
