    "details": "WEAPON / PHYSICAL INTERACTION / HANDS: VRGrenadeController.RepositionGrenadeThrow intercepts BaseGrenadeHandsController.method_9 for the local player and refuses launch until pinPulled. It reads SteamVR velocity, position and rotation, converts them through vrOffsetter and calls native vmethod_2 with the tracked origin/orientation, force and fuse-related arguments. Velocity above 0.1 m/s is multiplied by 1.5 and capped at 15; lower speed uses a forward-force fallback. Native player velocity is added only when withVelocity is set. A separate animation state bridge seeks the release portion, detects wrap, freezes briefly and calls the native drop-finished method to complete hand state.\n\nWEAPON / PHYSICAL INTERACTION / HANDS IMPLEMENTATION USE: Treat trajectory substitution and native animation completion as separate obligations. Preserve fuse/inventory ownership when changing release pose. Test slow release, fast throw, artificial locomotion and interrupted animation. This function explicitly queries the physical RightHand pose even though other input paths support handedness; verify that asymmetry before reusing it. The slow-release fallback is not a zero-force drop.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Supplied `SPT-VR-1.3.0.zip`, C# source audit dated 2026-09-07. Files: `Patches/Core/VR/VRGrenadeController.cs`, `Source/Controls/ControllerVelocity.cs`. The implementation paragraph describes recovered code; adaptation and validation guidance is identified separately.",
