    "details": "PHYSICAL INTERACTION / GESTURE / ARM IK / HANDS: EatingInteractionController separates food definitions, gesture state, latched hands, rig targets, props and synchronization. StepOpenPull maps trigger/pull/tilt progress into the native open clip; ScrubOpen seeks Animator.Play at normalized time while playback is frozen. Reach-taking measures depth and lateral displacement in an anchor frame and scrubs the use clip. Drink progress is conditional on mouth/tilt state. Rig.SubscribePinAfterIk attaches hand pins to FinalIK solver.OnPostUpdate because Player.LateUpdate can occur before the solver; latched hands target the object latch, otherwise the tracked rig target. Prop handling saves original parents/local transforms, repins after animation and restores them during teardown.\n\nPHYSICAL INTERACTION / GESTURE / ARM IK / HANDS IMPLEMENTATION USE: Reuse existing authored deformation and audio while allowing physical progress to drive the animation playhead. Own each transform at the final writer stage: animation, IK and render-only pins may run in different orders. Restore original hierarchy, solver hooks and state on every exit. Test partial opening, release/regrip, interrupted consumption and switching items.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Supplied `SPT-VR-1.3.0.zip`, C# source audit dated 2026-09-07. Files: `Source/Player/Interactions/Eating/EatingInteractionController.Gestures.cs`, `Source/Player/Interactions/Eating/EatingInteractionController.Rig.cs`, `Source/Player/Interactions/Eating/EatingInteractionController.Props.cs`. The implementation paragraph describes recovered code; adaptation and validation guidance is identified separately.",
