    "details": "PHYSICAL INTERACTION / GESTURE: DrainDrinkLive keeps time-derived consumption separate from total applied consumption because spoon bites may also consume the same item. Each time delta is capped to live remaining resource, small updates are chunked, and a final fractional remainder is applied so the bar can reach empty. ApplyConsumedNutrition reads HealthEffectsComponent energy/hydration entries, calls ActiveHealthController.ChangeEnergy/ChangeHydration with CutPiece(fraction), subtracts MaxResource*fraction from FoodDrinkComponent.HpPercent and raises the item refresh event. HpPercent is treated as resource units, not an ordinary 0-100 percentage. On error the function checks remaining resource rather than automatically discarding the item.\n\nPHYSICAL INTERACTION / GESTURE IMPLEMENTATION USE: When physical gestures take over timing, budget all consumption paths against the current resource and update the native UI model. Preserve the distinction between continuous progress and already-consumed totals. This implementation explicitly applies energy/hydration; it should not be described as replaying every possible native food effect. Test mixed bite/drink paths, partial use and floating-point remainder.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Supplied `SPT-VR-1.3.0.zip`, C# source audit dated 2026-09-07. Files: `Source/Player/Interactions/Eating/EatingInteractionController.cs`, `Source/Player/Interactions/Eating/EatingInteractionController.Gestures.cs`. The implementation paragraph describes recovered code; adaptation and validation guidance is identified separately.",
