    "details": "MULTIPLAYER / ARM IK / WEAPON: VRArmSync throttles at 0.05 seconds and expresses poses using chest.InverseTransformPoint and inverse(chest.rotation)*worldRotation. Empty hands send both hand poses. Held gun/knife/grenade sends WeaponRoot pose plus offhand pose and foregrip state; eating has a distinct packet with wrists, hashed prop names, visibility and per-layer animation hashes/times. ArmSyncApply executes after ObservedPlayer.LateUpdate: it reconstructs the weapon first, then re-solves hands at native grip markers or the free-hand pose, preserving firearm reload weights. Local chest-relative exponential smoothing uses rate 18, so body movement is not itself delayed. Empty-hand packets have a 0.4-second stale timeout. Weapon state uses a separate dictionary without that same receive-time gate. Firearm sync yields to native sprint animation.\n\nMULTIPLAYER / ARM IK / WEAPON IMPLEMENTATION USE: Replicate the representation that owns the interaction: weapon while armed, hands while empty, props during special actions. Smooth offsets relative to the body rather than smoothing the whole actor. Scope freshness rules per packet type; do not assume the arm timeout also covers weapons. Put receive/render support in an optional companion usable by flatscreen peers.\n\nSOURCE EVIDENCE: Supplied `SPT-VR-1.3.0.zip`, C# source audit dated 2026-09-07. Files: `ModSupport/VRArmSync.cs`, `FikaSync/Packets.cs`, `FikaSync/ArmSyncApply.cs`, `FikaSync/FikaVrSync.cs`. The implementation paragraph describes recovered code; adaptation and validation guidance is identified separately.",
