    "id": "seed_re5vr_case",
    "type": "case",
    "title": "Resident Evil 5 VR — D3D9 proxy / dgVoodoo2 D3D12 capture / OpenXR stereo",
    "game": "Resident Evil 5 (32-bit DX9 PC build, re5dx9.exe)",
    "engineFamily": "Capcom proprietary game engine (game-specific renderer hooks)",
    "renderAPI": "Direct3D 9 → dgVoodoo2 Direct3D 12 → OpenXR",
    "injectionMethod": "d3d9.dll proxy + dgVoodoo2 addon SampleAddon.dll + MinHook game hooks",
    "platform": "PC VR",
    "status": "alpha",
    "features": [
      "architecture",
      "stereoRendering",
      "cameraTracking",
      "input",
      "handsControls",
      "bodyIK",
      "weaponAiming",
      "physicalInteraction",
      "gestureInteraction",
      "uiProjection",
      "multiplayer"
    ],
    "featuresAudited": true,
    "summary": "A layered graphics conversion architecture: game scene renders into a double-wide per-eye backbuffer, dgVoodoo2 translates D3D9 to D3D12, an addon captures the finished target, and an OpenXR bridge submits it as a stereo pair.",
    "details": "ARCHITECTURE / GRAPHICS BRIDGE: VERIFIED FROM REPOSITORY DOCUMENTATION: the public `ResidentEvil5VR` repository describes the 32-bit `re5dx9.exe` path, a game-local `d3d9.dll` proxy, dgVoodoo2 translation from D3D9 to D3D12, and a dgVoodoo addon built as `SampleAddon.dll` that captures the completed D3D12 swapchain/backbuffer. The captured image is handed to the OpenXR bridge as a stereo pair. The README's repository layout names `RE5VR/src/proxy/`, `src/hooks/`, `src/render/`, `src/ui/`, `src/vr/openxr_bridge.cpp`, `src/vr/d3d12_addon_bridge.cpp`, and `addon/` as separate producers/consumers. This is a layered conversion bridge rather than a direct DX9 swapchain-to-OpenXR sharing path.\n\nRENDERING / STEREO: the README says the scene is rendered twice per frame into a single double-wide backbuffer, using each eye's camera and scissor rectangle. During VR, the game render size is switched to twice the runtime-recommended per-eye width by one eye height, allowing each half to use full eye resolution; the desktop mirror copies one eye rather than causing a third scene render. The OpenXR submission receives two eye textures through the addon bridge. The code/documentation describe native game scene rendering, not alternate-frame rendering. HUD shader bytecode is recognized and its output drawn once per eye onto a panel; a mono post-processing option avoids splitting bloom/light shafts between eyes. A port following this pattern must verify that the D3D12 addon’s captured target remains valid through OpenXR copy/submit and that resolution switches are restored when VR turns off.\n\nCAMERA / CULLING: repository docs describe hooks for the camera rig, game-action camera transitions and culling; the camera is made first-person while retaining the player body, and the head becomes visible again during selected action cameras to avoid a headless avatar. Camera heading is decoupled from aiming/walking direction so looking over the shoulder does not rotate gun/locomotion input. The README documents a configurable head prediction offset and FOV matching; these are documented features, not a universal guarantee about latency under every runtime.\n\nHANDS / IK / WEAPONS: the README documents 6DOF arm IK for shoulder/elbow/wrist each frame, controller wrist roll, support-hand orientation for two-handed weapons, holster reach/grab, hand reload via a belt-side pickup point, and hand stopping against characters/self rather than passing through. It documents a left-handed-character calibration switch for Sheva. These are sufficient for an implementation-method registry entry but the audit does not claim an independently inspected IK source algorithm or complete body-FBT implementation. The project reports arm-pose sync to co-op partners, but explicitly says online play has not been tested; networking behavior must be treated as documentation-only/untested.\n\nINPUT / UI: controllers map to the game’s ordinary gamepad input vocabulary, which means this is not by itself proof of native OpenXR action-based gameplay semantics. A repository menu uses Dear ImGui; `input_block.cpp` gates game input while the menu is active and ignores a button that is still held as the menu closes to prevent accidental shots/camera rotation. Native HUD/menu outputs are projected onto a panel; specialty title/organize screens remain listed issues. A captured desktop mirror displays one eye for streaming.\n\nEVIDENCE / LIMITS: VERIFIED FROM REPOSITORY DOCUMENTATION AND TREE: the official GitHub README describes the rendering bridge, resolution logic, feature list, repository modules and build layout. The public README labels v0.5.0a as active development, says online has not been tested, mentions the 32-bit address-space/4GB patch, partial manual reload support (pistols best supported), exclusive-fullscreen instability, some broken menu surfaces, and a WIP theatre-screen path. UNKNOWN HERE: exact per-function calling conventions and algorithmic internals beyond the documented module descriptions; this audit did not build or run the mod. Do not treat controller-as-gamepad as a fully semantic action architecture or its co-op arm sync as validated multiplayer support.\n\nREUSABLE IMPLEMENTATION GUIDANCE: use a translation/producer-consumer bridge when the game API is too old to share its native graphics device with OpenXR directly; treat target sizing, HUD capture and desktop mirror as explicit sub-systems; keep camera/gameplay heading separate from HMD looking; and block legacy input only during a VR overlay’s actual focus interval.",
    "blockers": "Repository documents v0.5.0a as active development. Online play is not tested; manual reload is strongest for pistols; 6DOF/hand-interaction maturity varies; some menus and exclusive-fullscreen transitions remain problematic. The audit did not build or run the mod, and algorithmic IK internals are not established here.",
    "sourceLinks": "https://github.com/SpreadTheBirb/ResidentEvil5VR, https://github.com/SpreadTheBirb/ResidentEvil5VR/blob/main/README.md, https://github.com/SpreadTheBirb/ResidentEvil5VR/tree/main/RE5VR/src/proxy, https://github.com/SpreadTheBirb/ResidentEvil5VR/tree/main/RE5VR/src/render, https://github.com/SpreadTheBirb/ResidentEvil5VR/tree/main/RE5VR/src/vr, https://github.com/SpreadTheBirb/ResidentEvil5VR/tree/main/RE5VR/addon",
    "submittedBy": "source-audit",
    "createdAt": "2026-10-10"
