    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE/DOCS: `camera_rig.hpp`, `scripted_camera.hpp`, `scripted_view.hpp`, `scripted_position.hpp` and `gameplay/campaign/sequences/camera_policies.hpp` separate head rotation (`fixed/pitch_roll/limited/free`), translation (`fixed/attenuated/tracked`), native script rotation (`override_view/additive/ignore`), native rotation axes, source pose/tag and one-time entry alignment. Game-thread adapters publish values; named-tag lookup occurs outside the tracking mutex, and camera composition doesn't retain native object pointers. Rotation composes once for the shared camera; eye offsets/projections remain per-eye. `roomscale_origin.hpp` rotates around the tracked head origin, compensates camera/hand/body/equipment space after accepted native yaw and uses bounded command-time history to avoid replay/double application.\n\nPATTERN: model camera as a prioritized policy/ownership decision, not a global “replace view angles” patch. Make tracking yaw, command yaw, script yaw, locomotion displacement and roomscale origin separate state. Scope entry alignment to an owner/lifecycle epoch and keep it pending until its tag is valid; invalidate it on load/recenter/relink, not on every poll. A scripted camera may accept native yaw but attenuate HMD translation, while a fixed optic may own both rotation and translation.\n\nLIMITS: scene policies explicitly list special sequences. Native collision/movement remains authoritative; this is not a full roomscale physics controller. Use mission evidence before generalizing a map-specific policy.",
