    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE: `gameplay/hands/pose_solver.hpp` has a 256-bone cap, explicit shoulder/elbow/wrist chains, named gun/tag/muzzle/rear-grip/laser bones and a 1.25 maximum arm stretch ratio. It validates finite lengths, parent topology and frames. A law-of-cosines solve targets hand position; the elbow pole comes from authored bend in the body frame, with an optional pole hint and source-plane fallback for degenerate geometry. `arm_plane_normal` retains authored anatomical axes for straight source arms; `orient_arm` transports upper and lower segments through one oriented bend plane rather than independently shortest-arc rotating them, which avoids sudden 360-degree elbow rolls. The pose is solved in temporary storage and copied atomically only after validation; owned weapon bones are not rewritten as ordinary arm descendants. `rig_builder.hpp` rejects duplicate/ambiguous/incompatible bone hierarchies instead of guessing.\n\nPATTERN: separate geometry solve from native model binding. Bind only a known rig/profile; clamp unreachable targets; make degenerate cases deterministic; update only the intended descendant chains; validate the entire result before mutation. A held weapon target is not automatically a full-body IK target. Overlord establishes bilateral arm solving and selected scripted upper-limb control, not full-body leg/waist tracking.\n\nTRANSFER: Reuse the solver mathematics where units/handedness are normalized. Rebuild the rig mapping per target game/model and preserve native body root, shoulders and non-arm bones unless those are explicitly authorized. Offline IK tests cannot prove final wrist fit or elbow comfort in the headset.",
