    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE/DOCS: `weapon_registry.hpp`, `weapon_registration.hpp`, `weapon_profiles.hpp`, `weapon_profile_binding.hpp`, `weapon_attachments.hpp`, and `weapons/<family>/profile.hpp` form the profile system. It checks model/topology/attachment roles/cardinality and muzzle requirements, exposes bounded/deduplicated capability views, and derives detachable-magazine, tube and break-action catalogs from the registration source of truth. Each assembly can provide grip and aim anchors, hand/finger pose sets, activity bones, loading points and separate primary/underbarrel modules, including each module's own feed/action/muzzle/ammo binding. Profiles are explicit because WeaponDef class flags and bone-name guesses are not a full mechanical specification.\n\nPATTERN: inventory identity and visual model are related but not identical. Admit a feature only when the current native weapon/attachment identity matches an audited profile; maintain a stable instance/revision across pickup, stow, draw and animation/model rebuild. Treat underbarrel equipment as a separate firing/loading module, not decoration on the rifle. Capability lists should reject overflow/duplicate registrations rather than silently truncate.\n\nLIMITS: reviewed catalog and unit tests do not mean every attachment, animation, dual-wield combination or weapon has passed headset acceptance. The weapon-architecture docs explicitly keep arbitrary mixed-weapon dual wield as a non-goal/pending boundary.",
