    "featuresAudited": true,
    "summary": "Derive the shot from a validated weapon muzzle, reject stale or obstructed geometry, compare-and-commit native ammo, settle mechanical state, then invoke the original bullet pipeline exactly once.",
    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE: `native_ballistics.cpp::initialize()` verifies masked instruction bytes for the bullet wrapper, weapon descriptors/spread path, weapon type, native trace and player-state firing gate, then initializes native ammunition access. `fire_owned()` is server-scheduler-only and checks cgame/player/command-time/state/focus/pause, validated finite muzzle geometry, native identity, supported firearm type, loaded ammo, muzzle distance, shield obstruction and an eye-to-muzzle `G_TraceCapsule`. It reads the original WeaponDef/spread values and rejects missing/out-of-range values. `native_ammunition::commit_carried()` performs expected-snapshot ammo validation/commit. The mechanical observer settles before the native bullet call because that call can synchronously trigger damage/scripts; `emitting` prevents reentry. Once native execution begins it is not rolled back/refunded as if the transaction were side-effect-free. The native function still owns damage, collision and scripts.\n\nPATTERN: treat a shot as a one-way transaction with a strict order: validate identity/context and geometry -> validate line of muzzle exit -> validate/debit ammo -> settle mechanical state -> enter native fire once -> observe result. The eye-to-muzzle test matters in VR because the tracked controller can put a muzzle through nearby cover while the eye remains behind it. Keep camera ray, controller aim ray, weapon muzzle and projectile gameplay separate. Store/revision-check the muzzle transform; a stale muzzle from the previous hand pose must not fire.\n\nLIMITS: byte signatures and offsets are exact-build-specific; no address should be copied to another executable without verification. This is guarded native fire integration, not custom ballistics or proof every attachment/shot scenario works.",
