    "featuresAudited": true,
    "summary": "Separate physical magazine/shell/slide intent from committed loaded/reserve ammunition; use profile-specific feed adapters, native-owner commits and identity-preserving ledgers.",
    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE/DOCS: `physical_reload_runtime.cpp`, `reload_item_runtime.cpp`, `native_ammunition.cpp`, `cylinder_runtime.cpp`, `tube_runtime.cpp`, `break_action_runtime.cpp`, `launcher_runtime.cpp`, and `underbarrel_runtime.cpp` separate detachable magazines, segmented shells/tubes, cylinders, break-actions, launchers and underbarrel feeds. Native ammo reads and writes are centralized in `native_ammunition`; expected state snapshots and carried weapon identity gate writes on the native server scheduler. Reload-item objects have their own physical ownership, world/waist supply, expiry/fall/refund policies. Weapon/carry identity and physical magazine presentation are distinct. Per-instance clip/mechanical ledger and generation identity are used to reconcile drop/pickup rather than automatically resetting a feed when the entity/model changes.\n\nPATTERN: the controller gesture only means *intent*. Commit requires a known weapon profile, correct current item, compatible hand lease, valid feed stage, reserve/capacity and still-current native weapon/ammo state. Mutate game ammo on its owner thread through one adapter; do not independently decrement ammo in a visual component, native hook and reload module. If native state changed externally or the owner changed, reconcile or reject without manufacturing rounds. Settle hand ownership before firing/reload callbacks so trigger/reload state cannot race in two domains.\n\nEVIDENCE CAVEAT: older `vr-weapon-interaction-architecture.md` text still calls a larger mechanical model a design target, while current modules and focused tests implement multiple feed adapters. Report each family as source-implemented/test-covered but do not treat every profile, campaign state or headset experience as accepted. Individual magazines with persistent rounds remain a stated non-goal.",
