    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE/DOCS: `ladder_scene.cpp` extracts bounded/incremental LOD0 indexed geometry from static or supported single-root script models and caches actual horizontal mesh edges; it doesn't fabricate rungs from bounds. Candidate and held contact points must still hit current `SURF_FLAG_LADDER` faces and pass visibility checks. `ladder_native.cpp` wraps the native detector and only suppresses native automatic ladder mode for an eligible player's physical-ladder branch. `ladder_runtime.cpp` uses a script-owned invisible non-solid carrier and native link/ground-reference operations. `free_climb.hpp` handles retained goals and two-hand averaging; `climb_collision.hpp` bounds/slide-sweeps the full player capsule. Server phase does gameplay traces/physics; renderer only previews the already bounded current pull segment.\n\nPATTERN: separate geometry discovery from contact admission and from movement authority. A nearby mesh edge is only a candidate; the native surface bit, occlusion, current entity/model generation and hand lease must also pass. The gameplay owner computes a collision-approved absolute body position; don't add delayed player deltas on a carrier that has already moved. Two hands average shared movement, and releasing a grip rebases remaining goals. Blocked/grounded motion is consumed rather than queued into a launch. Render prediction must never issue server traces or mutate physics.\n\nLIMITS: only known static/single-root forms admitted; animated/multi-model/unverified scaled meshes fall back to the native ladder path. Documentation records remaining headset fit, jitter/upper-rail and representative mission acceptance work.",
