    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE: `main.cpp` performs supported-binary/version checks and creates a known patched binary copy for the loader. Native hook adapters use `utils::hook_validation::verify_masked_bytes` for expected call-site/wrapper bytes. Renderer stereo admission includes execution-context census evidence; an unknown D3D11 context or opaque command list that cannot be accounted for can block production stereo. OpenVR texture admission checks resource device, generation, dimensions, format, usage/flags and lifetime. Weapon adapters similarly verify shot/spread/trace entry bytes before `fire_owned` becomes eligible. Diagnostics preserve rejection/status reasons rather than crashing through unknown object state.\n\nPATTERN: treat every signature/offset/ABI, D3D texture, bone topology, weapon profile and native entity identity as an explicit capability contract. Perform preflight validation, install atomically where possible, and keep the native/fallback path when the invariant is not established. A byte match is necessary, not proof of all object state; pair it with runtime state/pipeline checks. Keep the exact build and validation evidence in diagnostics.\n\nLIMITS: this protection is version-specific and cannot make an unsupported game binary compatible. Fail-closed gates may leave tracking live while stereo stays disabled, which is better than claiming an invalid pair.",
