    "summary": "Convert native weapon kick pitch ranges into a per-shot impulse on the VR weapon pose, accumulate automatic fire, and recover exponentially toward tracking aim.",
    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE/DOCS: `weapon_recoil_tuning.hpp` centralizes weapon family aliases/scales and type guards; recoil documentation/source records shot-time posture, support-grip ownership and recoil state. A confirmed native shot produces upward weapon pitch. The receiver, firing wrist/fingers and support hand via forearm IK move as a coherent assembly; raw controllers and HMD remain unchanged. Native pitch velocity endpoints may be descending or span zero, so both are handled; extreme/non-finite data is rejected. Base posture strengths are standing 3x, crouched 2x, prone 1x; eligible unsupported standing/crouching weapons receive a 4x penalty under default `vr_recoilPenalty=long`; prone suspends that penalty. Stored pitch decays exponentially with a 0.22 s time constant and caps at 55 degrees.\n\nPATTERN: trigger recoil from accepted shots, not input presses; record it at the shot timestamp; apply it to the physical weapon pose with receiver/hand coupling; allow tracked aim to become the recovery target. Separate posture and support-grip policy from base native recoil lookup. Validate out-of-range values and put per-family adjustments in a table, not in all fire hooks.\n\nLIMITS: current model uses hip pitch values and does not simulate horizontal recoil, the per-shot random sample, full ADS interpolation, or native acceleration/reduced-kick sequences. The tuning has device/weapon acceptance requirements.",
