    "summary": "Keep H2 movement/collision authoritative and map VR intent into existing command paths; let selected climb/vehicle/story adapters own only the movement dimensions they explicitly need.",
    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE/DOCS: `controller_component.cpp` translates left-stick direction into native usercmd axes relative to horizontal HMD heading, right stick into configurable smooth/snap yaw, and button actions into native sprint/jump/stance/bind routes. It gates movement/turn/fire according to scripted camera/scene permissions, turret/vehicle/climbing state and focus/tracking. Smooth turn doesn't reset temporal history every command; discontinuous snap/camera cuts do. `roomscale_origin.hpp` compensates world space around the current HMD; it doesn't implement alternative game collision or velocity. Ladder carrier/free-climb and specific vehicle adapters use separate native ownership, so ordinary movement does not run concurrently with their special control loops.\n\nPATTERN: add intent at the earliest correct native command boundary, then let the game's movement/grounding/collision code perform the move. Decompose movement ownership by axis/action and scene phase; don't have camera, locomotion and vehicle code each write native yaw. Clear/rebase history on genuine discontinuities and neutral-arm after context changes. Special adapters should be explicit and fall back to native mode for unsupported asset geometry.\n\nLIMITS: no general full-body physical locomotion or arbitrary climb-any-surface guarantee follows from the current ladder/Cliffhanger adapters.",
