    "summary": "Keep the game as authority for inventory, damage and entity lifecycle, while preserving VR mechanical state only through validated identity/generation records.",
    "details": "VERIFIED FROM SOURCE/DOCS: weapon carry uses native inventory/world ownership and typed holster/body slots; ammo is centralized through `native_ammunition`; reload item and clip/mechanical ledger code tracks physical representations separately from the native weapon/entity. Reused entity indices or a model swap do not establish the same item identity by themselves. World pickup/drop still delegates native entity/physics/notifies and the mod reconciles held/reload ledger by generation/revision. Native bullet, collision, ladder surface, story script and vehicle link operations are likewise preserved as game-owned authority boundaries.\n\nPATTERN: don't let the VR layer become a competing inventory or damage engine. Maintain a compact mapping `(native identity, generation/revision) -> VR-only mechanical/presentation state`; validate it when reacquiring, and reconcile if external game code changes weapon/inventory/mission state. Separate commit operations from cosmetic item motion. A commit that can trigger scripts is a one-way boundary; after it starts, blindly refunding state can duplicate side effects.\n\nLIMITS: a generation ledger is only as good as the identity and lifecycle witnesses. Unreviewed attachment, checkpoint or save/load transitions must be tested; persistence of magazines with individual remaining-round counts is explicitly a non-goal.",
