    "summary": "Source-engine VR mod using a D3D9 proxy DLL, native engine hooks, SteamVR/OpenVR-style action bindings, tracked two-handed weapon handling, custom hand rendering, roomscale prediction, and optional VR pose networking.",
    "details": "Source audit of the supplied l4d2vr-master tree. The project is a native 32-bit Windows mod for Left 4 Dead 2's Source/D3D9 renderer, not a Unity/Unreal plugin. The client DLL bootstraps through dllmain.cpp and separates game/engine hooks, VR lifecycle and tracking, render interception, controller/weapon aiming, custom hands, and optional pose transport. hooks_render.inl contains substantial render-path instrumentation and eye/pass handling; hooks_createmove.inl bridges VR state into Source user commands; vr_tracking.inl and vr_aiming.inl handle tracking/camera/aim logic; vr_roomscale_prediction.inl handles roomscale/render-camera deltas. A dedicated pose protocol and optional server-side relay are included. See CODE_AUDITS for category-by-category evidence and limitations.",
    "blockers": "Source-specific offsets and signatures are build-sensitive. The README warns about VAC risk and recommends -insecure; do not assume arbitrary public servers support all VR-only interactions. README says interactions/throwables can still require face-aiming except on VR-only servers. The supplied tree is a snapshot; compatibility with current game/runtime builds is not established by source inspection alone. Some low-level behavior is distributed across large .inl files and should be validated against exact call sites before porting.",
