    "summary": "Track explicit render-pass identity so eye-specific logic does not accidentally affect scopes, mirrors, or unrelated passes.",
    "details": "RENDERING — Source-audit of supplied `l4d2vr-master` source tree; code paths listed below are primary evidence. Portable recipes are recommendations, not claims that the project implements every suggested safeguard. `hooks/hooks_render.inl` defines `HooksNekoPostPass` categories including `MainEye`, `Scope`, and `RearMirror`, and maintains probe state including pass, eye index, sequence and takeover state. The file includes D3D9 surface/texture probes and temporal-state diagnostics gated to the main-eye path. This is evidence of explicit pass classification and diagnostics, not proof of a custom OpenXR swapchain or compositor.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: Model render context as a tagged state (pass kind, eye, frame/sequence ID, target surface). Set and clear that context around known engine render boundaries. Gate modifications by the intended pass instead of treating every render callback as an eye. When correlating temporal artifacts, associate the source surface, eye and frame serial; log mismatches rather than sampling arbitrary global state.\n\nVALIDATION: Exercise both eyes, scope view, rear mirror, menus/loading and repeated renders within one frame. Confirm diagnostic probes cannot alter render state in normal operation and restore all D3D9 state/resources on every error path. The exact final composition remains engine/runtime-owned unless separately demonstrated.",
    "blockers": "The pass taxonomy and probes are project-specific. Do not generalize it into claims of OpenXR projection-layer submission or late latching.",
