    "summary": "Keep the player’s roomscale reference separate from render-camera correction to avoid applying head displacement twice.",
    "details": "CAMERA / COORDINATE SPACES — Source-audit of supplied `l4d2vr-master` source tree; code paths listed below are primary evidence. Portable recipes are recommendations, not claims that the project implements every suggested safeguard. `vr/vr_roomscale_prediction.inl` exposes `VR::GetAimRenderCameraDelta()` and maintains explicit pending roomscale movement and visual-correction state. Comments explain that tracking can update faster than server user-command processing and that replacing a pending movement request must cancel the visual displacement paired with the replaced request. The architecture distinguishes world movement from visual correction rather than treating both as one camera offset.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: Name coordinate spaces explicitly (tracking, player-yaw-local, world, render-camera). Convert physical HMD displacement into a gameplay movement request, then pair that request with a corresponding render compensation. Queue the pair atomically; when a newer request supersedes the old one, cancel the old visual term too. Apply accepted server correction once and clear stale state on reset, teleport, death/spectator transitions or tracking discontinuity.\n\nVALIDATION: Move physically while stationary in-game, push the stick during roomscale movement, hit a wall, lose/reacquire tracking, recenter, and transition spectator→live. Check that neither camera drift nor doubled translation accumulates. Exact gameplay policy remains specific to this mod.",
