    "details": "INPUT / DEVICE SUPPORT — Source-audit of supplied `l4d2vr-master` source tree; code paths listed below are primary evidence. Portable recipes are recommendations, not claims that the project implements every suggested safeguard. `SteamVRActionManifest/action_manifest.json` is accompanied by distinct bindings for Knuckles, Oculus Touch and Vive Cosmos. `vr/vr_process_input.inl` reads action state and translates it into game-level behavior. This structure separates the action vocabulary from device-specific physical controls.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: Define semantic actions such as move, turn, primary attack, reload, use, jump, crouch and recenter in a runtime manifest. Keep each controller profile in a separate binding file; map device-specific buttons/axes to the same semantic names. In gameplay code, consume actions rather than checking controller model/button indices. Provide explicit invalid/disconnected action-state handling and a recenter/reset path.\n\nVALIDATION: Load every binding profile, inspect unbound actions, verify left/right hand roles, and test analog dead zones and pressed-versus-held semantics. The supplied manifests prove SteamVR action/binding assets; they do not prove OpenXR action-set support.",
    "blockers": "SteamVR/OpenVR-oriented assets are present; do not claim OpenXR compatibility from these manifests alone.",
