    "featuresAudited": true,
    "summary": "Sample tracking on the appropriate input/render path, but consume gameplay-changing requests at the engine command boundary.",
    "details": "THREAD / STATE OWNERSHIP — Source-audit of supplied `l4d2vr-master` source tree; code paths listed below are primary evidence. Portable recipes are recommendations, not claims that the project implements every suggested safeguard. `vr/vr_object_pull.inl` comments explicitly distinguish controller input on the render/input path from client entity access consumed by `CreateMove` on the Source client thread. It defines tracking samples and trace-result structures, rather than assuming a live entity pointer can safely be used from any callback. `vr/vr_roomscale_prediction.inl` similarly queues world movement and paired visual correction for later consumption.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: At the runtime-facing stage, capture a bounded, validated pose/action sample containing the transform, timestamp/tick and validity. Publish the sample or a small request object; do not carry unstable engine entity pointers across threads. On the game/client command thread, revalidate the entity and world query, decide whether the action is allowed, then apply the native operation. Give requests a sequence/generation so stale requests can be dropped after death, level change or hand-role change.\n\nVALIDATION: Stress different frame and tick rates, long frames, level transitions, stale samples and entity destruction. Confirm a request cannot dereference a pointer acquired on another thread and that the newest tracking sample replaces stale intent predictably.",
    "blockers": "The source demonstrates this separation in selected paths; it does not establish that every global in the mod is thread-safe.",
    "sourceLinks": "https://github.com/keyou91/l4d2vr/blob/master/L4D2VR/vr/vr_object_pull.inl, https://github.com/keyou91/l4d2vr/blob/master/L4D2VR/vr/vr_roomscale_prediction.inl, https://github.com/keyou91/l4d2vr/blob/master/L4D2VR/hooks/hooks_createmove.inl",
    "submittedBy": "source-audit",
