    "details": "MULTIPLAYER POSES — Source-audit of supplied `l4d2vr-master` source tree; code paths listed below are primary evidence. Portable recipes are recommendations, not claims that the project implements every suggested safeguard. `hooks/hooks_world_pose.inl` comments state that tracking samples remain player-yaw-local on the wire and are resolved against the current `ModelRenderInfo_t`. `vr_pose_protocol.h` contains wire-only definitions shared by the client relay and optional dedicated-server plugin, intentionally avoiding Source SDK types. The protocol includes packed tracked-pose data and quantization constants.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: Choose and document a stable reference frame for networked poses. Serialize only transport-safe scalar/packed data; keep engine pointers and SDK objects out of the protocol header. At receive time, validate packet/schema and pose age, resolve local-space samples against the current entity yaw/origin, and then construct the visual transform. A relative frame can avoid retransmitting absolute world positions, but it requires a clearly defined reference-frame update policy.\n\nVALIDATION: Test yaw rotation between packet creation and rendering, delayed/out-of-order packets, recenter, respawn, entity reuse, protocol mismatch and missing hands. Do not interpolate across a teleport or identity change.",
