    "details": "BODY / IK / REMOTE PRESENTATION — Source-audit of supplied `l4d2vr-master` source tree; code paths listed below are primary evidence. Portable recipes are recommendations, not claims that the project implements every suggested safeguard. `hooks/hooks_world_pose.inl` describes layering a visual head/upper-body/dual-arm solve over Source’s final model setup. It explicitly distinguishes first-person viewmodel arms from the world-model upper-arm-to-hand chain, and includes arm/finger layout structures and rest-chain caches. This supports an upper-body/arm presentation technique; it does not prove full-body leg IK.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: Let the game produce its normal model pose first. Resolve tracked head/hand targets in the model’s current reference frame, then solve only the intended visual bones (clavicle/upper arm/forearm/hand) while preserving the exact tracked hand target. Cache validated bone-name/index layouts and rest-chain transforms, with a fallback when a model lacks required bones. Keep remote visual reconstruction separate from gameplay hitboxes and native animation authority.\n\nVALIDATION: Check different survivor models, missing/fallback finger bones, animation changes, third-person distance, network packet loss and first-person/world-model separation. Confirm the VR overlay does not mutate authoritative collision or claim leg/pelvis tracking absent from source.",
