    "details": "HANDS / RENDERING — Source-audit of supplied `l4d2vr-master` source tree; code paths listed below are primary evidence. Portable recipes are recommendations, not claims that the project implements every suggested safeguard. `vr_hands/vr_hand_renderer_d3d9.cpp` implements D3D9 shared-resource setup, texture and mesh resource creation, vertex/pixel shader compilation, bone constants and stencil handling. It defines a bounded shader-bone count and distinct world/viewmodel depth handling. `vr_hands/vr_hand_system.cpp` contains separate scene and viewmodel aspect calculations and `ReprojectScenePointToViewmodelLayer`, with comments explaining why reusing scene aspect for a viewmodel-bound hand causes drift.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: Separate hand asset/skeleton data from GPU resource lifetime. Create device resources lazily, validate shader/resource creation, and release/rebuild them on device reset. Treat first-person viewmodel hands and world-space hands as different render layers with different projection/depth rules; do not reuse a scene projection blindly for a weapon-bound hand. Keep stencil/occlusion manipulation scoped and restore D3D9 state.\n\nVALIDATION: Test D3D device reset, missing/invalid texture, shader compilation failure, different aspect ratios, both eyes, weapon/viewmodel occlusion, near-camera hands and low-light scenes. This code is a custom D3D9 hand-rendering path, not evidence of runtime-owned hand meshes or OpenXR swapchains.",
