    "details": "WEAPON AIMING / COORDINATE SPACES — Source-audit of supplied `l4d2vr-master` source tree; code paths listed below are primary evidence. Portable recipes are recommendations, not claims that the project implements every suggested safeguard. `vr/vr_tracking.inl` contains `VR::ResolvePavlovTwoHandedAimBasis`, with vector normalization, dot products, hand-delta checks and a source-units-per-meter parameter. `vr/vr_aiming.inl` contains guarded entity and weapon reads that matter when aim state is queried from render contexts. The two-handed helper is evidence of a basis-solving routine; exact game-by-game use should be followed through its call sites before asserting all weapons use it.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: Treat dominant-hand grip transform, support-hand position, weapon forward axis and muzzle transform as distinct values. Use the dominant hand to anchor the grip, derive a forward direction from the support/dominant geometry according to the chosen weapon convention, reject near-zero hand separation and non-finite vectors, and build an orthonormal basis before converting it into engine angles. Apply weapon-specific grip/muzzle offsets after the basis is stable. Keep projectile/native fire direction separate from the rendered hand mesh.\n\nVALIDATION: Test hands nearly coincident, extreme wrist angles, hand crossing, left-handed mode, recenter, weapon swap and model-specific muzzle offsets. Verify the actual call site and native shot path before claiming spread, recoil or damage semantics.",
