    "details": "THROWING / PHYSICAL INTERACTION — Source-audit of supplied `l4d2vr-master` source tree; code paths listed below are primary evidence. Portable recipes are recommendations, not claims that the project implements every suggested safeguard. `hooks/hooks_throwables.inl` defines pose-history recording and `ManualThrowEstimateReleaseVelocity`, including a release tick, velocity-window tick count, peak-velocity blend and a nominal server tick duration. It contains finite-vector checks, velocity magnitude clamping, expected weapon/kind state and pending-throw preparation/reset helpers. These are direct code-level signs of a bounded estimate and explicit release-state management.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: Sample hand position in a stable tracking/player-relative frame with tick identity. At release, estimate velocity over a bounded history, reject invalid/discontinuous samples, clamp extreme magnitudes, and decide explicitly whether player locomotion is inherited. Transfer the item back to the native throwable/game entity once, then clear history and pending state so a single release cannot launch twice. Preserve native fuse, damage, inventory and server rules.\n\nVALIDATION: Stationary drop, quick throw, long hold, moving while throwing, snap turn before release, tick hitch, tracking reset, weapon swap during wind-up and duplicate release callbacks. The exact blend/window constants should be read from the current source and tuned per game; no generic formula is implied.",
