    "details": "OBJECT INTERACTION — Source-audit of supplied `l4d2vr-master` source tree; code paths listed below are primary evidence. Portable recipes are recommendations, not claims that the project implements every suggested safeguard. `vr/vr_object_pull.inl` defines `ObjectPullTrackingSample`, `ObjectPullClientTraceResult`, and helper routines for reading entity origins, collision bounds and ray/AABB intersections. Its opening comments distinguish render/input-path tracking from client entity access consumed by `CreateMove`. This shows a staged object-pull implementation with explicit trace-result and sample state, rather than a direct unconstrained controller-to-entity transform.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: Convert a controller ray into a candidate query, use a broad-phase bounds test to cheaply reject irrelevant entities, then perform the game-supported trace/eligibility checks. Treat a candidate as provisional: revalidate entity identity, support, distance and current interaction state on the gameplay thread before applying movement/force. Separate visual targeting from accepted interaction and make cancel/invalid-target states explicit.\n\nVALIDATION: Aim through thin geometry, target moving/deleted entities, switch weapons/hands, move out of range, lose tracking and change maps. Verify that broad-phase bounds are only a filter, not a replacement for native collision/interaction rules.",
