    "details": "MULTIPLAYER / PROTOCOL — Source-audit of supplied `l4d2vr-master` source tree; code paths listed below are primary evidence. Portable recipes are recommendations, not claims that the project implements every suggested safeguard. `vr_pose_protocol.h` states that its wire-only definitions are shared by the client DLL’s built-in listen relay and optional dedicated-server plugin, and deliberately contain no Source SDK types. It defines packed tracked-pose and wire-packet structures plus bit readers/writers and quantization constants. `l4d2vr_pose_server.cpp` implements server-plugin callbacks and per-client protocol/sequence/decode/ack state.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: Put fixed-width, explicitly versioned packet fields in a header that has no dependency on engine classes. Validate packet length, version, supported feature flags and sequence before updating client state. Keep server SDK adaptation in a separate translation unit/plugin, and bound retries/state per player slot. Encode coordinate units and quantization in the schema, not in undocumented call-site assumptions.\n\nVALIDATION: Old/new protocol mismatch, truncated packet, invalid bit count, sequence wrap, client disconnect/reconnect in reused slots, missing acknowledgements and listen-server versus dedicated-server paths. Keep visual pose replication separate from gameplay authority; remote cosmetic pose should not become a source of hit registration.",
