    "featuresAudited": true,
    "summary": "Use a dedicated pose-waiter thread in queued mode, publish coherent snapshots, and fall back without blocking the game thread.",
    "details": "FRAME TIMING / POSE ACQUISITION — VERIFIED SOURCE: `vr/vr_lifecycle_pose_hud.inl` implements `VR::PoseWaiterThreadMain`, `VR::ReadPoseWaiterSnapshot`, and `VR::UpdatePosesAndActions`. The waiter is enabled when `mat_queue_mode != 0`; it calls SteamVR `WaitGetPoses`, publishes a fixed-size pose array under an atomic sequence counter (odd while writing, even when complete), signals an event, and optionally logs success/error rates. In queued mode the main path reads the latest published snapshot and uses a non-blocking `GetDeviceToAbsoluteTrackingPose` prediction fallback if the waiter has not published yet. Non-queued mode calls `WaitGetPoses` directly. `UpdatePosesAndActions` then updates the SteamVR action state and advances an action-state frame serial.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD: Separate runtime pacing from the engine’s render worker only when the engine’s queueing mode requires it. Publish a whole pose snapshot with a sequence/lock-free consistency protocol; never let consumers observe a partially copied pose array. Keep a non-blocking startup fallback and validate the prediction horizon. Associate the consumed pose with a submission/frame token so diagnostics can reveal duplicate or stale poses. Coordinate thread enable/disable and lifetime carefully: a detached worker must not outlive the runtime objects it reads.\n\nVALIDATION: Exercise `mat_queue_mode` zero and nonzero, early startup before the first snapshot, compositor errors, tracking loss, fast head motion, device/runtime shutdown and high queue load. Compare waiter success rate against HMD frequency and confirm no deadlock or render-thread stall. This source shows SteamVR timing/pacing coordination; it does not by itself prove a custom OpenXR late-latch stage or a universal predicted-display-time pipeline.",
    "blockers": "This is a SteamVR-specific queued-render adaptation. Detached-thread lifecycle and runtime shutdown require careful auditing beyond the snapshot algorithm.",
    "sourceLinks": "https://github.com/keyou91/l4d2vr/blob/master/L4D2VR/vr/vr_lifecycle_pose_hud.inl, https://github.com/keyou91/l4d2vr/blob/master/L4D2VR/vr/vr_lifecycle_update.inl",
