    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Hooks/Registry.cpp` registers hooks from static constructors but stores the head in a function-local static to avoid initialization-order loss, then sorts by stage/order before installation. Stages include PreDevice, Boot and PostStereo. `Stereo/DetourRegistry.cpp` does the same for engine detours. `Stereo/EngineRvas.hpp` is an explicitly documented table of verified Cyberpunk2077.exe offsets rather than scattered constants, while individual patches check expected instruction bytes before modification.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Create named installation stages around lifecycle boundaries that actually matter to the target engine. Keep every absolute address/signature in one build table with discovery notes. At each patch site verify the expected bytes or structural invariant, log ok/disabled/FAILED distinctly, and let a rejected patch disable only its dependent subsystem. This gives reverse-engineered VR code a traceable compatibility contract instead of optimistic writes into changed binaries.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test a known supported executable, then intentionally alter one expected byte/RVA and verify only that hook fails. Verify static registration order changes do not alter final hook order. On a new game build, require re-verification of the centralized table before enabling patches.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Hooks/Registry.cpp`, `src/Stereo/DetourRegistry.cpp`, `include/Stereo/EngineRvas.hpp`, `include/Utils/AobScanner.hpp`, `src/Main.cpp`.",
