    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `OpenXRManager.cpp` requires `XR_KHR_D3D12_enable`, queries OpenXR graphics requirements, and creates the XR session using the Cyberpunk process’s captured `ID3D12Device` and `ID3D12CommandQueue`. It creates PRIMARY_STEREO views plus LOCAL and VIEW reference spaces. Runtime selection remains OpenXR: SteamVR support is implemented by selecting SteamVR’s OpenXR runtime manifest before instance creation, not by adding a separate OpenVR compositor path.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Hook graphics creation early enough to retain the engine device/queue, then initialize XR against those exact objects. Keep runtime selection before `xrCreateInstance`; enumerate extensions before assuming optional depth support. This avoids cross-device copies and keeps the game renderer authoritative while XR owns headset presentation.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Validate adapter/device identity, D3D12 graphics requirements, queue lifetime, runtime switching before instance creation, and teardown order. Test runtime failure without leaving stale D3D objects or an active session. Do not call an OpenVR runtime-selection helper evidence of an OpenVR rendering backend.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Runtimes/OpenXRManager.cpp`, `src/Main.cpp`, `src/Runtimes/OpenXRCapture.cpp`.",
