    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Camera/ImagePoseIdentity.cpp` and the OpenXR capture/submit path maintain identity for rendered resources. The existing source audit records `StoreRenderEyePose`/rendered-pose queues keyed by engine sequence and matching MAIN/VRCAM capture serials. The identity is not just a pointer tag: resource reuse is accounted for so a recycled D3D object address cannot silently inherit a previous frame’s pose label. Recentered game-relative camera poses are converted back to the raw LOCAL-space form expected by OpenXR submission.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Assign a monotonically meaningful frame/eye identity at render ownership, not at submit. Store render pose, tracking-origin serial and eye identity beside the image lease. Reject or fall back when the two eye serials do not belong together. When the game uses a recentered coordinate basis but the compositor expects runtime-local space, explicitly reverse the recenter transform before submitting the render pose.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Stress GPU lag, capture-buffer reuse, recenter events, repeated frames and missing one-eye captures. A CPU frame number alone is insufficient if the GPU can overwrite a shared resource before submission; verify identity follows the actual resource generation/lease.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Camera/ImagePoseIdentity.cpp`, `include/Camera/ImagePoseIdentity.hpp`, `src/Runtimes/OpenXRCapture.cpp`, `src/Runtimes/OpenXRPresent.cpp`, `src/Runtimes/OpenXRFrameLoop.cpp`.",
