    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Stereo/FrameGraph.cpp` and companion stereo modules observe REDengine’s per-view feature bits and graph behavior. The source audit records that REDengine regenerates those flags each frame, so VRCAM-required groups must be reasserted at the writer. The project separates per-view needs such as culling/depth/composition from frame-global or shared resources; simply copying MAIN state or rerunning every node caused eye disagreements and missing dependencies.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — For each engine graph feature, identify whether it is (a) a per-view producer that must run, (b) a per-view consumer whose prerequisite must exist, or (c) frame-global state that should be shared. Instrument MAIN and second-view feature masks and node execution, then patch the authoritative per-frame writer rather than a one-time initialization value.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Validate daylight/interiors, scanner/vision modes, dynamic weather, effects and any state that changes graph feature bits. Check both missing producer failures and accidental duplicate frame-global work. Treat “feature flag present” and “valid resource produced for this view” as separate questions.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Stereo/FrameGraph.cpp`, `include/Stereo/FrameGraphFeatures.hpp`, `src/Stereo/NodeDispatch.cpp`, `include/Stereo/EngineRvas.hpp`.",
