    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Stereo/ViewReuse.cpp` exists specifically to coordinate resources that REDengine naturally treats as shared/once-per-frame. The source audit documents examples including sun/shadow cascades, foliage/wind, environment/composition and other resources whose independent second-eye execution can either waste work or leave the two views on different global state. Other data such as view-dependent depth/culling must remain per-eye.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Build a classification table for render products: frame-global reusable, view-dependent, or view-dependent consumer of shared global data. For reusable products, transfer or reference the completed MAIN result at the precise engine seam expected by VRCAM. For view-dependent products, rerun with VRCAM matrices. Avoid “copy all” and “rerun all” because both erase important ownership distinctions.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Profile correctness before performance. Verify shared resources are complete before VRCAM consumes them, are not mutated concurrently, and remain valid when render order changes. Compare temporal consistency and GPU cost across weather, foliage, shadows and vision effects.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Stereo/ViewReuse.cpp`, `src/Stereo/FrameGraph.cpp`, `src/Stereo/Grading.cpp`, `src/Stereo/VisionLayer.cpp`, `include/Stereo/EngineRvas.hpp`.",
