    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Stereo/Dlss.cpp` plus `Hooks/Ngx.cpp`/resolution hooks route VRCAM through separate Streamline/DLSS view state. The source audit explicitly identifies reuse of MAIN’s temporal/upscaler viewport as invalid for true stereo because history from one eye would feed the other. The implementation also coordinates feature-group selection and per-view dimensions when MAIN uses DLSS.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Treat temporal history as part of view identity. Every eye needs its own history key/context, jitter sequence interpretation, dimensions and reset policy. If a third-party temporal system is keyed by “viewport”, create or route a distinct second-eye viewport instead of only changing camera matrices around one shared history object.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test camera motion, disocclusion, resolution changes, DLSS on/off, menu transitions and history reset. Look specifically for ghost trails that jump between eyes or converge toward the other eye’s previous frame.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Stereo/Dlss.cpp`, `src/Hooks/Ngx.cpp`, `src/Hooks/DlssRes.cpp`.",
