    "summary": "Clock full-body solving to the engine animation batch rather than Present so repeated pose-apply passes see one coherent skeleton solution.",
    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Hooks/AnimPose.cpp` detours the pose-apply path and measures/identifies fresh animation epochs. The existing source audit records that one fresh VRIK solve is cached for relevant bones and replayed on later pose passes in the same batch. Two-hand authored-pose capture occurs before VR writes, and ownership transitions invalidate the cache so a pose from the previous owner is not replayed after control changes.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Find the engine’s true animation evaluation boundary. On the first local-player pose application in a new epoch, solve tracked-body IK and cache the resulting bone transforms. On duplicate render/animation passes for that same epoch, replay the cached result rather than sampling controllers again or recomputing against a different camera state. Invalidate on ownership/lifecycle transitions.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Log pose-apply timings and epoch IDs. Test multiple render views, pause/resume, camera takeovers, weapon/vehicle transitions and any path that applies the same skeleton more than once. Look for one-eye/one-pass body phase errors.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Hooks/AnimPose.cpp`, `src/Anim/CharacterRig.cpp`, `include/Anim/VrikState.hpp`.",
    "blockers": "The epoch detector and pose buffer layout are REDengine-specific, but the solve-once/replay principle is broadly portable.",
