    "summary": "Use HMD height/position to place hips and bend the torso/legs without making head yaw implicitly own the body root.",
    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Anim/CharacterRig.cpp` contains the body placement solver described in the existing source audit: capture foot positions, infer physical squat/drop from HMD height with filtering/deadzone/clamp, move the hips under the head anchor while retaining torso length, perform repeated spine/neck correction to reduce head residual, solve both legs back to planted feet with forward-knee constraints, and rotate the head bone to the VR camera. Body yaw remains a separate heading policy.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Separate root placement, vertical crouch mapping and facing direction. Preserve pre-solve foot contacts as IK targets, reposition pelvis/torso to satisfy the tracked head, then solve legs back to the contacts. Distribute remaining head error across spine/neck rather than telescoping one bone. Publish solved landmarks for interaction systems instead of making every script rediscover them.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test standing, crouching, leaning, turning in place, uneven animation states and large height calibration differences. Verify body-root yaw does not chase every small HMD yaw and that feet do not drift when the player bends.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Anim/CharacterRig.cpp`, `src/Hooks/AnimPose.cpp`, `include/Anim/VrikState.hpp`.",
