    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `CharacterRig.cpp` scales upper-arm/forearm rest translations toward measured user arm length within safety clamps. Its arm solve uses body axes to construct an anatomical bend plane, handles cross-body and near-extension cases, adds clavicle/shoulder protraction for far reaches, distributes twist and applies wrist calibration after converting XR controller pose into avatar/model space. The hand target can also be stopped/clamped by interaction ownership such as reload.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Calibrate skeleton segment lengths first, then solve target position in a stable body/model frame. Let the shoulder girdle contribute near maximum reach; calculate an elbow pole from torso anatomy rather than a fixed world vector; smooth the pole/twist and handle near-singular extension. Keep raw tracked pose global, and apply calibration/collision constraints only in the arm consumer.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test cross-body reach, hand behind/above head, near-full extension, two-handed weapons, handedness and abrupt tracking loss. Verify calibration changes the avatar arm geometry rather than merely multiplying controller offset.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Anim/CharacterRig.cpp`, `src/Hooks/AnimPose.cpp`, `include/Anim/VrikState.hpp`.",
