    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Hooks/RoomscaleMove.cpp`, `Hooks/OnFootMoveXY.cpp` and camera/body-heading code separate consumed physical HMD displacement from engine/world locomotion. Movement sources can be Game, HMD, LeftHand or RightHand; hand-relative movement uses controller aim orientation. Optional physical body rotation writes headset yaw through the engine heading channel so mesh/collision/weapon/movement share facing while the HMD remains an additive view transform.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Maintain explicit values for tracking-space displacement, the portion already consumed into player movement, render-camera offset and body heading. Convert roomscale delta into the engine’s native movement/heading interface, then remove only the consumed component from camera anchoring. For yaw, feed intentional physical rotation to the body/engine while never feeding that body yaw back into the headset view.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test walking around the play area, artificial movement at the same time, snap/smooth turning, hand-relative locomotion, recenter and transitions into vehicles/cinematics. Look for double translation, orbiting camera or body yaw feedback loops.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Hooks/RoomscaleMove.cpp`, `src/Hooks/OnFootMoveXY.cpp`, `src/Hooks/BodyYawFollow.cpp`, `include/Hooks/RoomscaleMove.hpp`.",
