    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Hooks/WeaponAim.cpp` and `docs/cp2077-hitscan-physicalray-muzzle.md` identify `gameEffectObjectProvider_PhysicalRay::Execute` callsites as the production firearm ray path. The wrapper calls the original evaluator, verifies the effect belongs to the local player weapon, sanity-checks the current VR muzzle against the native origin, moves origin to the muzzle, snapshots both the native cone center and muzzle forward, and rotates each already-generated ray by the camera-cone→barrel-cone rotation.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Hook as late as possible after the game has generated authoritative projectile/spread rays. Preserve each ray’s angular offset inside the cone, but rotate the entire cone to the physical barrel and move origin to the live muzzle. Filter for the local player/weapon and reject stale muzzle data using spatial/time invariants. Leave ammo, fire rate, damage and hit processing native.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test single-ray guns, shotguns, hip fire, ADS, recoil, weapons with unusual muzzle offsets and stale/unarmed weapon state. A shotgun should retain pellet distribution, not collapse into one ray. Validate that foreign PhysicalRay users are untouched.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Hooks/WeaponAim.cpp`, `docs/cp2077-hitscan-physicalray-muzzle.md`.",
