    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Anim/TwoHandGrip.cpp` captures one native two-hand animation frame with VRIK disabled and stores support-wrist transform relative to the primary wrist plus finger rotations in per-weapon INI files. Runtime reconstructs that support point from the live primary wrist, previews by proximity and commits on a fresh/unspent grip edge. Aim correction uses support-hand tracking error with smoothing/deadzone/caps and leverage weighting: long rifle baselines can steer strongly; short pistol baselines deliberately receive less angular authority.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Provide a calibration/capture mode that samples the target game’s authored hold before VR overwrites the pose. Store the relative support transform and finger pose as weapon data. At runtime arbitrate grip ownership before activation, then constrain/steer the weapon based on support-hand error. Scale steering authority by hand separation to prevent centimeters of noise from creating huge pistol rotations.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test capture/reload of configs, weapon aliases/reskins, grip/release edges, very short and long baselines, support hand crossing the primary hand, and conflicts with reload/holster/wheel interactions. Ensure a single grip press cannot be spent by two systems.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Anim/TwoHandGrip.cpp`, `include/Anim/TwoHandGrip.hpp`, `mods/config/CyberpunkVR_TwoHandGrip_lexington.ini`.",
