    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Anim/Recoil.cpp` implements a damped spring where shots add velocity impulse and integration uses bounded small substeps; per-weapon/class tuning and two-hand support scale the response. `AdsEyeAlign.cpp`/`AdsMuzzleStabilizer.cpp` adapt the game’s authored ADS transition around an eye/weapon pivot without letting it redirect the live muzzle. `Shaders/sight_reflex_ps.hlsl` computes reticle displacement from eye-to-sight geometry so the dot behaves like a collimated optic rather than a decal stuck to glass.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Apply firing impulse to the visual/IK weapon owner, not to head/camera orientation. Integrate a damped spring with stable timestep behavior and let support-hand leverage attenuate it. For ADS, preserve native state/animation but reconcile it against the actual dominant-eye line. For reflex optics, calculate reticle direction from the eye and sight optical frame and pass stable world-size/calibration data explicitly.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test rapid automatic fire at variable FPS, one- vs two-hand grip, entering/exiting ADS, head translation around the sight and temporal-upscaler jitter. The reticle should stay optically collimated while the gun recoils independently of the HMD.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Anim/Recoil.cpp`, `src/Anim/AdsEyeAlign.cpp`, `src/Anim/AdsMuzzleStabilizer.cpp`, `src/Shaders/sight_reflex_ps.hlsl`.",
