    "featuresAudited": true,
    "summary": "Put magazine/slide interaction logic in a reusable geometry-driven core, keep weapon dimensions/poses as data, and split genuinely different mechanisms instead of filling one universal state machine with exceptions.",
    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `mods/cet/CyberpunkVRPort_Reload/reload/reload.lua` is the shared state/geometry layer. It consumes live weapon-rig part transforms from the native pose bridge and models magazine grab/extraction/carry/insertion/drop plus slide/palm interaction. Magazine travel follows the well/path; slide travel projects hand motion onto the measured slide/barrel axis. Finger poses, wrist lock/hand stop and ownership state keep the hand attached to the manipulated part. Weapon-specific modules provide geometry/pose data. `revolver.lua` treats a cylinder/speedloader/cases as a distinct mechanism rather than forcing it through box-magazine logic.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Define a small mechanism state machine around physical thresholds, not animation time. Convert controller/hand motion into weapon-local space; constrain moving parts to their mechanical rails/axes; keep ammo/action/audio commits at explicit state transitions. Store per-weapon wells, paths and hand/finger poses as data. When a weapon family has a different topology—such as a revolver—provide a mechanism adapter with the same external ownership contract.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test grabbing before/after empty, dropping and regrabbing a magazine, partial insertion, slide manipulation, handedness, tracking discontinuity and grip conflicts. Verify native auto-reload cannot race the physical state. For revolvers, test individual case retention/ejection and speedloader transitions separately.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `mods/cet/CyberpunkVRPort_Reload/reload/reload.lua`, `mods/cet/CyberpunkVRPort_Reload/reload/revolver.lua`, `src/Hooks/AnimPose.cpp`, `src/Anim/ReloadPose.cpp`.",
    "blockers": "Physical reload coverage is per tuned weapon/mechanism; do not claim arbitrary weapons work without configuration.",
    "sourceLinks": "https://github.com/dariulone/cyberpunk-vr-port, https://github.com/dariulone/cyberpunk-vr-port/blob/main/mods/cet/CyberpunkVRPort_Reload/reload/reload.lua, https://github.com/dariulone/cyberpunk-vr-port/blob/main/mods/cet/CyberpunkVRPort_Reload/reload/revolver.lua, https://github.com/dariulone/cyberpunk-vr-port/blob/main/src/Hooks/AnimPose.cpp, https://github.com/dariulone/cyberpunk-vr-port/blob/main/src/Anim/ReloadPose.cpp",
