    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `CyberpunkVRPort_Weapon/init.lua` gates blade contact on physical weapon velocity. `mods/redscript/CyberpunkVRPort_Melee/vrport_melee.reds` models the blade as a finite segment, caps physical reach below flat-game lunge range, samples candidate NPC body heights and chooses the closest valid contact with a per-target repeat cooldown. It then builds the weapon’s own `Attack_GameEffect`; a damage-calculation bridge restores the intended queued melee damage before native armor/crit/marker processing when script-initiated attacks would otherwise be zeroed.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Separate recognition from authority. First require credible swing speed and segment/body contact. Once accepted, call the target game’s normal attack/effect system using the equipped weapon record, instigator and contact direction rather than applying raw health damage. Add a minimal compatibility bridge only where the engine rejects an otherwise native effect because its original button-driven state machine was bypassed.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test slow touches, fast slash through multiple targets, repeat contact on one NPC, reaching to holster, blocked/armored targets and failure to create the native attack effect. Confirm effects/reactions/damage numbers come from native combat rather than duplicate VR code.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `mods/cet/CyberpunkVRPort_Weapon/init.lua`, `mods/redscript/CyberpunkVRPort_Melee/vrport_melee.reds`, `mods/redscript/CyberpunkVRPort_WeaponUp/vrport_weapon_up.reds`.",
