    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `CyberpunkVRPort_Holster/init.lua` consumes solved/published wrist-to-body anchors for right hip, left hip and back zones. It supports visual-slot classification and a simpler fixed-slot mode, applies proximity/cooldown/cross-body rules, and suppresses holster logic during states such as smoking. The wider source audit records that wheel/reload/carry interactions can pre-claim the grip so reaching for another system does not accidentally equip or unequip a weapon.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Publish stable torso/hip/back landmarks from the body solver. Define holster zones relative to those landmarks, not head/world coordinates. Before interpreting a grip edge as holster intent, run a central ownership/arbitration check against every higher-priority interaction. Once a zone transition is accepted, invoke the game’s native equipment action and impose a short cooldown/intent window so the same reach cannot become a melee swing.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test crouch/lean/body-yaw changes, cross-body reaches, seated/vehicle states, simultaneous reload or steering grips, rapid enter/exit of a zone and visual-vs-simple slot mode. Confirm body calibration moves zones with the avatar rather than with the HMD alone.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `mods/cet/CyberpunkVRPort_Holster/init.lua`, `src/Anim/CharacterRig.cpp`, `src/Anim/TwoHandGrip.cpp`, `src/Anim/WheelGrab.cpp`.",
