    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `CyberpunkVRPort_Ladder/init.lua` explicitly says Lua bridges ladder geometry/state only; tracking and grip movement remain native. It reads the game `LadderDescription` and optional finisher-rail transforms and publishes them through `SetVRLadderState`/`SetVRLadderTopRails`. `LadderInput.cpp` builds both hands from the same latched body/view frame, locates closest rail/rung/top-rail contacts, uses grip hysteresis (release/press thresholds), anchors a held palm, rejects implausible tracking jumps, constrains the VRIK hand to the physical contact, and converts vertical tracked pull into a bounded native MoveY axis via `Climber::Debt()`. Near the top, an intentional upward pull can request the game’s own ladder finish rather than teleporting the player.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Use the game’s authoritative ladder object to supply geometry and state. Convert tracked palm contact into explicit anchors only on a grip edge within a capture radius. While held, constrain visual IK to the anchor and accumulate player movement from controller motion in tracking space, then feed that as the game’s ordinary ladder input. Use origin/sequence freshness, grip hysteresis and motion discontinuity rejection. Let the native state machine perform top exit.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test one- and two-hand climbing, grabbing rails vs rungs, releasing/regrabbing, moving the HMD while holding, tracking recenter/origin change, ladder switching, top finisher rails and manual stick input. The code cancels physical override when ordinary movement input is significant, which is an important coexistence check.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `mods/cet/CyberpunkVRPort_Ladder/init.lua`, `src/Natives/Ladder.cpp`, `src/Hooks/LadderInput.cpp`, `include/Runtimes/LadderClimbing.hpp`, `include/Anim/LadderRungWrist.hpp`.",
    "blockers": "This is integrated with Cyberpunk’s existing ladder state machine and geometry. It is not a general climb-any-surface physics system.",
