    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `CyberpunkVRPort_Swimming/init.lua` bridges swimming/water state and merges only four actions (MoveY, ToggleSprint, Jump, Dive) for the local player. `SwimmingInput.cpp` samples both controller hands and head from one gesture frame. `SwimmingGesture.hpp` implements a Reach→Pull→Recover breaststroke with timing, travel, symmetry, velocity and discontinuity checks, a separate downward two-hand `AscendStroke`, provisional early propulsion that expires quickly if a stroke aborts, and boost hysteresis based on sustained filtered hand velocity. `SwimmingMovement.hpp` redirects native horizontal swim velocity by tracked head heading while intentionally preserving the game’s existing vertical component/buoyancy.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Recognize gestures in tracking/head-local space so artificial/world movement does not invent a stroke. Require a stable ready/reach pose, then evaluate actual bilateral travel and velocity over time; reject tracking jumps and origin changes. Emit semantic native actions for a bounded glide, boost or ascent instead of directly setting world position. Preserve native vertical movement when the game already includes pitch/buoyancy to avoid double-applying it.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test gentle/fast strokes, aborted partial pulls, moving the head without moving hands, tracking jumps, surface/diving transitions, existing fast-swim state, manual stick input and pausing. Verify a partial early pull cannot grant a full glide and that boost does not chatter on noisy velocity samples.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `mods/cet/CyberpunkVRPort_Swimming/init.lua`, `src/Natives/Swimming.cpp`, `src/Hooks/SwimmingInput.cpp`, `include/Runtimes/SwimmingGesture.hpp`, `include/Runtimes/SwimmingMovement.hpp`.",
