    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Anim/WheelGrab.cpp` detects hand proximity/grip at the authored wheel. When a hand grabs, the implementation captures/restores the animation-driven hand and returns that arm to the native driving pose, including rest translations so VRIK arm scaling/protraction does not distort the wheel contact. Steering derives from controller geometry with one- and two-hand variants, deadzone/lock-angle policy and wheel-hub horn proximity. Source comments emphasize that merely skipping an IK solve is insufficient if cached solves or translation writes still replay afterward.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — For interactions where authored animation is visually superior, transfer ownership at the consumer layer. On grab, restore the native/rest transforms required by the animation, invalidate any cached VR solve for that limb, and stop all competing translation/rotation writes. Continue using controller positions to compute semantic steering/horn/fire intent, then blend/reacquire VRIK on release.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test one-hand/two-hand steering, hand entering/leaving the grab zone, weapon drawn while driving, throttle latch/trim, horn proximity and rapid grab transitions. Specifically verify no stale same-tick VRIK cache reattaches the arm after ownership was handed to animation.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Anim/WheelGrab.cpp`, `include/Anim/WheelSteering.hpp`, `include/Anim/TrackedWheelSteering.hpp`, `src/Hooks/XInput.cpp`.",
