    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `OpenXRManager.cpp` creates separate grip pose and aim pose actions plus stick, trigger, grip, click, face and menu actions with bindings for several controller profiles. `Hooks/XInput.cpp` merges VR state into Cyberpunk’s XInput path and contains gameplay-specific policies such as movement tiers, sprint detent, crouch/dash, scanner gesture and quickhack paging. Its comments explicitly require menus and braindance to receive raw controller behavior because VR remaps that are helpful in gameplay can steal buttons from UI.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Define semantic XR actions first, then translate them at the legacy game-input boundary instead of patching every gameplay system. Maintain an input-ownership state machine: gameplay remaps/chords active only when gameplay owns input; UI/cinematic modes get ordinary controller values. Use head/hand-local geometry only for gestures, with hysteresis/debounce, and keep the actual action press in the native button channel.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test opening/closing UI while buttons are held, scanner gesture near its boundary, sprint/crouch/dash state changes, quickhack paging and simultaneous physical interactions. Verify one gesture cannot leak a remapped button into a menu after the UI becomes active.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Runtimes/OpenXRManager.cpp`, `src/Hooks/XInput.cpp`.",
