    "summary": "Integrate frame interpolation inside the existing VR capture/presentation pipeline, consuming the game’s own depth/motion resources and preserving eye/pose identity instead of bolting on an unrelated compositor.",
    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — Audited from the user-supplied `cyberpunk-vr-port-main` snapshot. `Framegen/Inputs.cpp` hooks Streamline input publication and copies matching depth/motion resources into per-view records keyed by frame, pose, origin, view and command queue. `Framegen/Generator.cpp` uses FidelityFX frame interpolation/depth-motion inputs; the NVIDIA backend replaces only the optical-flow stage with NVIDIA OFA while retaining FidelityFX interpolation. `Framegen/Presenter.cpp` requires matching stereo/input identity, resets on tracking-origin/projection discontinuity, generates a midpoint image when two valid real frames can be interpolated, and assigns the synthetic frame a pose interpolated between the two real eye poses. It reuses the port’s existing color captures—no private XR swapchain or second presenter. `Framegen.cpp` adds output pacing plus real/generated/repeat CPU/GPU/VRAM telemetry.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION METHOD — Capture interpolation inputs at the renderer point where their camera constants, depth and motion vectors are known, and key them to the same identity used for the color frame. Generate only when consecutive frames have compatible origin/projection and both eyes have valid inputs. Keep interpolation as a producer feeding the existing XR presenter; do not create a competing submission loop. For a synthetic midpoint, use a corresponding midpoint render-pose estimate rather than labeling it with either endpoint’s pose.\n\nVALIDATION / TRANSFER — Test scene cuts/reset, menus/untracked views, projection/origin change, missing depth or motion vectors, GPU queue mismatch, low game FPS and external frame-generation layers. Verify generated/repeated/real frames are separately counted and that interpolation disables cleanly when inputs become incompatible.\n\nSOURCE FILES — `src/Framegen/Inputs.cpp`, `src/Framegen/InputCopy.cpp`, `src/Framegen/Generator.cpp`, `src/Framegen/Presenter.cpp`, `src/Framegen/Framegen.cpp`, `cmake/NativeFramegen.cmake`.",
