    "details": "VERIFIED SOURCE — The supplied Skate3VR snapshot describes an unofficial VR mod built on the native PC recompilation of Skate 3, not a conventional emulator plugin. ReXGlue converts the Xbox 360 PowerPC program into host C++ ahead of time; the resulting program still runs against a ReXGlue guest environment that provides Xbox-style virtual memory, XEX/module loading, kernel/XAM services, graphics, audio, input and export/function dispatch. Skate-specific host code then overrides selected recompiled guest functions, captures scene state, drives a native renderer, and connects the D3D12 guest-output seam to OpenXR. The Windows VR launch path forces D3D12, native scene rendering and VR together.\n\nRENDER / XR — A Skate-specific patch extends ReXGlue’s native guest-output context with the real D3D12 device, direct queue, output resource and resource state. OpenXR is created against that same device/queue. The runtime waits/begins the XR frame, locates stereo views at predicted display time, the native renderer produces a double-wide stereo image, and a post-submit callback copies each half into the corresponding OpenXR swapchain before `xrEndFrame`.\n\nXBOX 360 / INPUT — OpenXR controller state is deliberately translated back into Xbox 360-compatible controls. The final path publishes a `SyntheticGamepadState` directly into ReXGlue’s XAM input layer so Skate receives sticks, triggers and buttons through its existing `XamInputGetState` behavior. This preserves the original game’s controller-facing semantics instead of replacing every gameplay action with a VR-specific API.",
